#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:101
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Jails"
msgid "Thick Jails"
msgstr "Jails"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:108
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A thick jail is a traditional form of FreeBSD Jail.  In a thick jail, a "
"complete copy of the base system is replicated within the jail's "
"environment.  This means that the jail has its own separate instance of the "
"FreeBSD base system, including libraries, executables, and configuration "
"files.  The jail can be thought of as an almost complete standalone FreeBSD "
"installation, but running within the confines of the host system.  This "
"isolation ensures that the processes within the jail are kept separate from "
"those on the host and other jails."
msgstr "厚型 jail 是 FreeBSD Jail 的传统形式。在厚型 jail 中，基本系统的完整副本会复制到 jail 环境中。这意味着 jail 拥有独立的 FreeBSD 基本系统实例，其中包括库、可执行文件和配置文件。可以将 jail 看作几乎完整的独立 FreeBSD 安装，但它运行在宿主系统的限制范围内。这种隔离可确保 jail 中的进程与宿主系统及其他 jail 中的进程彼此分离。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:110
#, fuzzy
msgid "Advantages of Thick Jails:"
msgstr "厚型 jail 的优点："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:112
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"High degree of isolation: Processes within the jail are isolated from the "
"host system and other jails."
msgstr "高度隔离：jail 中的进程与宿主系统及其他 jail 隔离。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:113
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Independence: Thick jails can have different versions of libraries, "
"configurations, and software than the host system or other jails."
msgstr "独立性：厚型 jail 可以使用与宿主系统或其他 jail 不同版本的库、配置和软件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:114
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Security: Since the jail contains its own base system, vulnerabilities or "
"issues affecting the jail environment will not directly impact the host or "
"other jails."
msgstr "安全性：由于 jail 包含自己的基本系统，影响 jail 环境的漏洞或问题不会直接影响宿主系统或其他 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:116
#, fuzzy
msgid "Disadvantages of Thick Jails:"
msgstr "厚型 jail 的缺点："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:118
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Resource overhead: Because each jail maintains its own separate base system, "
"thick jails consume more resources compared to thin jails."
msgstr "资源开销：由于每个 jail 都维护自己的独立基本系统，厚型 jail 比薄型 jail 消耗更多资源。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:119
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Maintenance: Each jail requires its own maintenance and updates for its base "
"system components."
msgstr "维护：每个 jail 都需要单独维护和更新其基本系统组件。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:121
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:765
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Creating Jails"
msgid "Thin Jails"
msgstr "建立 Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:130
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A thin jail shares the base system from a template, using either OpenZFS "
"snapshots or NullFS mounts.  Only a minimal subset of the base system is "
"duplicated for each thin jail, resulting in less resource consumption "
"compared to a thick jail.  The two mechanisms behave differently once the "
"jails exist.  With the OpenZFS method, each thin jail is created as a clone "
"of a template snapshot: an independent copy-on-write copy that shares "
"unchanged blocks with the template but diverges as it is modified.  Later "
"changes to the template do not propagate to existing clones, and each clone "
"is maintained and updated individually, much like a thick jail.  With the "
"NullFS method, each thin jail mounts the template read-only at runtime, so "
"the base system is shared live and updating the template updates every jail "
"that mounts it.  This shared, read-only base is also what gives NullFS thin "
"jails less isolation and independence than thick jails, since changes in the "
"shared components affect every jail using them simultaneously."
msgstr "薄型 jail 通过 OpenZFS 快照或 NullFS 挂载共享模板中的基本系统。每个薄型 jail 只需复制基本系统的最小子集，因此与厚型 jail 相比，资源消耗更少。这两种机制在 jail 创建后会以不同方式运行。使用 OpenZFS 时，每个薄型 jail 都会创建为模板快照的克隆：这是一个独立的写时复制副本，与模板共享未更改的数据块，但会在修改时产生差异。之后对模板所做的更改不会传播到现有克隆；每个克隆都需要单独维护和更新，与厚型 jail 类似。使用 NullFS 时，每个薄型 jail 会在运行时以只读方式挂载模板，因此基本系统是实时共享的，更新模板也会更新所有挂载该模板的 jail。正是这种共享的只读基本系统，使 NullFS 薄型 jail 的隔离性和独立性低于厚型 jail，因为共享组件的更改会同时影响所有使用它们的 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:132
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In summary, a FreeBSD Thin Jail is a type of FreeBSD Jail that replicates a "
"substantial portion, but not all, of the base system within the isolated "
"environment."
msgstr "总而言之，FreeBSD 薄型 Jail 是一种 FreeBSD Jail，它会在隔离环境中复制基本系统的大部分内容，但并非全部。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:134
#, fuzzy
msgid "Advantages of Thin Jails:"
msgstr "薄型 jail 的优点："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:138
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Resource Efficiency: Thin jails are more resource-efficient compared to "
"thick jails.  Since they share most of the base system, they consume less "
"disk space and memory.  This makes it possible to run more jails on the same "
"hardware without consuming excessive resources."
msgstr "资源效率：与厚型 jail 相比，薄型 jail 的资源效率更高。由于它们共享大部分基本系统，因此占用的磁盘空间和内存更少。这使得同一硬件能够运行更多 jail，而不会消耗过多资源。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:140
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Faster Deployment: Creating and launching thin jails is generally faster "
"compared to thick jails.  This can be particularly advantageous when rapidly "
"deploying multiple instances."
msgstr "部署更快：与厚型 jail 相比，创建和启动薄型 jail 通常更快。在需要快速部署多个实例时，这尤其有利。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:143
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Unified Maintenance: With the NullFS method, where the thin jails share a "
"single read-only copy of the base system, updates and maintenance of common "
"base system components (such as libraries and binaries) only need to be done "
"once on the template.  This simplifies the maintenance process compared to "
"maintaining an individual base system for each thick jail.  OpenZFS-clone "
"thin jails do not share this benefit: because each clone is independent, "
"updates must be applied to each jail individually, as with a thick jail."
msgstr "统一维护：使用 NullFS 时，薄型 jail 共享基本系统的单个只读副本，因此只需在模板上更新和维护一次常见的基本系统组件（例如库和二进制文件）。与为每个厚型 jail 单独维护基本系统相比，这简化了维护流程。OpenZFS 克隆型薄型 jail 不具备此优势：由于每个克隆都是独立的，必须像厚型 jail 一样逐个更新。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:145
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Shared Resources: Thin jails can more easily share common resources such as "
"libraries and binaries with the host system.  This can potentially lead to "
"more efficient disk caching and improved performance for applications within "
"the jail."
msgstr "共享资源：薄型 jail 可以更轻松地与宿主系统共享库和二进制文件等常见资源。这有可能提高磁盘缓存效率，并改善 jail 中应用程序的性能。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:147
#, fuzzy
msgid "Disadvantages of Thin Jails:"
msgstr "薄型 jail 的缺点："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:150
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Reduced Isolation: The primary disadvantage of thin jails is that they offer "
"less isolation compared to thick jails.  With the NullFS method in "
"particular, jails share a live copy of the template's base system, so "
"vulnerabilities or issues affecting those shared components could "
"potentially impact multiple jails simultaneously."
msgstr "隔离性降低：薄型 jail 的主要缺点是其隔离性低于厚型 jail。尤其是使用 NullFS 时，jail 会共享模板基本系统的实时副本，因此影响这些共享组件的漏洞或问题可能同时影响多个 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:151
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Security Concerns: The reduced isolation in thin jails could pose security "
"risks, as a compromise in one jail might have a greater potential to affect "
"other jails or the host system."
msgstr "安全问题：薄型 jail 的隔离性较低，可能带来安全风险，因为一个 jail 遭到入侵后，可能更容易影响其他 jail 或宿主系统。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:153
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Dependency Conflicts: If multiple thin jails require different versions of "
"the same libraries or software, managing dependencies can become complex.  "
"In some cases, this might require additional effort to ensure compatibility."
msgstr "依赖项冲突：如果多个薄型 jail 需要同一库或软件的不同版本，依赖项管理可能会变得复杂。在某些情况下，可能需要额外工作来确保兼容性。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:154
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Compatibility Challenges: Applications within a thin jail might encounter "
"compatibility issues if they assume a certain base system environment that "
"differs from the shared components provided by the template."
msgstr "兼容性挑战：如果应用程序假设薄型 jail 具有某种基本系统环境，而该环境与模板提供的共享组件不同，应用程序可能会遇到兼容性问题。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:156
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1405
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Jails"
msgid "Service Jails"
msgstr "Jails"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:162
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A service jail shares the complete filesystem tree directly with the host "
"(the jail root path is [.filename]#/#) and as such can access and modify any "
"file on the host, and shares the same user accounts with the host.  By "
"default it has no access to the network or other resources which are "
"restricted in jails, but they can be configured to re-use the network of the "
"host and to remove some of the jail-restrictions.  The use case for service "
"jails is automatic confinement of services/daemons inside a jail with "
"minimal configuration, and without any knowledge of the files needed by such "
"service/daemon.  Service jails are available since FreeBSD 15.0."
msgstr "服务型 jail 直接与宿主系统共享完整的文件系统树（jail 根路径为 [.filename]#/#），因此可以访问和修改宿主系统上的任何文件，并与宿主系统共享相同的用户账户。默认情况下，它无法访问网络或 jail 中受限制的其他资源，但可以将其配置为重复使用宿主系统的网络，并移除部分 jail 限制。服务型 jail 的用途是以最少的配置自动将服务/守护进程限制在 jail 中运行，而无需了解此类服务/守护进程所需的文件。FreeBSD 15.0 起提供服务型 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:164
#, fuzzy
msgid "Advantages of Service Jails:"
msgstr "服务型 jail 的优点："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:166
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Zero Administration: A service jail ready service needs only one config line "
"in [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#, a service which is not service jails ready "
"needs two config lines."
msgstr "无需管理：对于已支持服务型 jail 的服务，只需在 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中添加一行配置；对于尚未支持服务型 jail 的服务，则需要添加两行配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:167
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Resource Efficiency: Service jails are more resource efficient than thin "
"jails, as they do not need any additional disk space or network resource."
msgstr "资源效率：服务型 jail 比薄型 jail 更节省资源，因为它们不需要额外的磁盘空间或网络资源。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:168
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Faster Deployment: Creating and launching service jails is generally faster "
"compared to thin jails if only distinct services/daemons shall be jailed and "
"no parallel instances of the same service/daemon is needed."
msgstr "部署更快：如果只需将不同的服务/守护进程分别置于 jail 中，且不需要同一服务/守护进程的多个并行实例，那么创建和启动服务型 jail 通常比薄型 jail 更快。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:170
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Shared Resources: Service jails share all resources such as libraries and "
"binaries with the host system.  This can potentially lead to more efficient "
"disk caching and improved performance for applications within the jail."
msgstr "共享资源：服务型 jail 与宿主系统共享所有资源，例如库和二进制文件。这有可能提高磁盘缓存效率，并改善 jail 中应用程序的性能。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:171
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Process Isolation: Service jails isolate a particular service, it can not "
"see processes which are not a child of the service jail, even if they run "
"within the same user account."
msgstr "进程隔离：服务型 jail 会隔离特定服务，使其无法看到并非该服务型 jail 子进程的进程，即使这些进程使用相同的用户账户运行也是如此。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:173
#, fuzzy
msgid "Disadvantages of Service Jails:"
msgstr "服务型 jail 的缺点："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:175
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Reduced Isolation: The primary disadvantage of service jails is that they "
"offer no filesystem isolation compared to thick or thin jails."
msgstr "隔离性降低：服务型 jail 的主要缺点是，与厚型或薄型 jail 相比，它不提供文件系统隔离。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:176
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Security Concerns: The reduced isolation in service jails could pose "
"security risks, as a compromise in one jail might have a greater potential "
"to affect everything on the host system."
msgstr "安全问题：服务型 jail 的隔离性较低，可能带来安全风险，因为一个 jail 遭到入侵后，可能更容易影响宿主系统上的所有内容。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:180
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most of the configuration of jails which is discussed below is not needed "
"for service jails.  To understand how jails work, it is recommended to "
"understand those configuration possibilities.  The details about what is "
"needed to configure a service jail are in the crossref:jails[service-jails-"
"config, Service Jails] section."
msgstr "下文讨论的大多数 jail 配置都不适用于服务型 jail。要了解 jail 的工作原理，建议先了解这些配置选项。服务型 jail 所需配置的详细信息请参见 crossref:jails[service-jails-config, 服务型 Jail] 一节。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:182
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1043
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Jails"
msgid "VNET Jails"
msgstr "Jails"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:187
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A FreeBSD VNET jail is a virtualized environment that allows for the "
"isolation and control of network resources for processes running within it.  "
"It provides a high level of network segmentation and security by creating a "
"separate network stack for processes within the jail, ensuring that network "
"traffic within the jail is isolated from the host system and other jails."
msgstr "FreeBSD VNET jail 是一种虚拟化环境，可隔离并控制其中运行的进程所使用的网络资源。它通过为 jail 中的进程创建独立的网络协议栈，提供高级别的网络分段和安全性，确保 jail 内的网络流量与宿主系统及其他 jail 隔离。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:190
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In essence, FreeBSD VNET jails add a network configuration mechanism.  This "
"means a VNET jail can be created as a Thick or Thin Jail."
msgstr "本质上，FreeBSD VNET jail 增加了一种网络配置机制。这意味着 VNET jail 可以创建为厚型或薄型 jail。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:192
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1208
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Creating Jails"
msgid "Linux Jails"
msgstr "建立 Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:197
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A FreeBSD Linux Jail is a feature in the FreeBSD operating system that "
"enables the use of Linux binaries and applications within a FreeBSD jail.  "
"This functionality is achieved by incorporating a compatibility layer that "
"allows certain Linux system calls and libraries to be translated and "
"executed on the FreeBSD kernel.  The purpose of a Linux Jail is to "
"facilitate the execution of Linux software on a FreeBSD system without "
"needing a separate Linux virtual machine or environment."
msgstr "FreeBSD Linux Jail 是 FreeBSD 操作系统的一项功能，可在 FreeBSD jail 中使用 Linux 二进制文件和应用程序。此功能通过集成兼容层实现，该兼容层可将某些 Linux 系统调用和库转换为 FreeBSD 内核能够执行的形式。Linux Jail 的目的是让 Linux 软件能够在 FreeBSD 系统上运行，而无需单独的 Linux 虚拟机或环境。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:199
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Time Zone Configuration"
msgid "Host Configuration"
msgstr "设置时区"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:202
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before creating any jail on the host system it is necessary to perform "
"certain configuration and obtain some information from the host system."
msgstr "在宿主系统上创建任何 jail 之前，需要执行某些配置并从宿主系统获取一些信息。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:204
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It will be necessary to configure the man:jail[8] utility, create the "
"necessary directories to configure and install jails, obtain information "
"from the host's network, and check whether the host uses OpenZFS or UFS as "
"its file system."
msgstr "需要配置 man:jail[8] 工具，创建配置和安装 jail 所需的目录，从宿主系统获取网络信息，并检查宿主系统使用的是 OpenZFS 还是 UFS 文件系统。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:208
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The FreeBSD version running in the jail can not be newer than the version "
"running in the host."
msgstr "jail 中运行的 FreeBSD 版本不能高于宿主系统中运行的版本。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:211
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Jail Utility"
msgstr "Jail 工具"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:214
#, fuzzy
msgid "The man:jail[8] utility manages jails."
msgstr "man:jail[8] 工具用于管理 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:216
#, fuzzy
msgid "To start jails when the system boots, run the following commands:"
msgstr "要在系统启动时启动 jail，请运行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:221
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# sysrc jail_enable=\"YES\"\n"
"# sysrc jail_parallel_start=\"YES\"\n"
msgstr "# sysrc jail_enable=\"YES\"\n# sysrc jail_parallel_start=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:226
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With `jail_parallel_start`, all configured jails will be started in the "
"background."
msgstr "启用 `jail_parallel_start` 后，所有已配置的 jail 都会在后台启动。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:230
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"By default every jail with an entry in the configuration files is started at "
"boot.  To start only selected jails, list their names in `jail_list`:"
msgstr "默认情况下，配置文件中有条目的每个 jail 都会在启动时启动。若要只启动选定的 jail，请在 `jail_list` 中列出它们的名称："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:234
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sysrc jail_list=\"www db\"\n"
msgstr "# sysrc jail_list=\"www db\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:239
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The names in `jail_list` are separated by spaces and must match the jail "
"names defined in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# or [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/"
"#.  Only the listed jails are started at boot, and they are started in the "
"order given, so any jail left out of `jail_list` has to be started by hand.  "
"When `jail_list` is left empty, all jails defined in the configuration files "
"are started."
msgstr "`jail_list` 中的名称以空格分隔，且必须与 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 或 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/# 中定义的 jail 名称一致。启动时只会启动列出的 jail，并按给定顺序启动，因此未列入 `jail_list` 的 jail 必须手动启动。若 `jail_list` 为空，则配置文件中定义的所有 jail 都会启动。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:241
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To stop the jails in the reverse of their `jail_list` order at shutdown, set "
"`jail_reverse_stop`:"
msgstr "若要在关闭时按 `jail_list` 中顺序的逆序停止 jail，请设置 `jail_reverse_stop`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:245
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "# sysrc jail_reverse_stop=\"YES\"\n"
msgstr "named_enable=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:253
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With `jail_parallel_start` enabled, jails start in the background and the "
"`jail_list` order is no longer guaranteed.  When one jail must be running "
"before another starts, express that relationship with the `depend` parameter "
"in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# instead of relying on list order.  A jail's "
"dependencies are created automatically before it starts, and stopped in the "
"opposite order, regardless of `jail_list`.  The `depend` parameter is "
"described in crossref:jails[jail-configuration-files,Jail Configuration "
"Files]."
msgstr "启用 `jail_parallel_start` 后，jail 会在后台启动，`jail_list` 中的顺序将不再得到保证。如果某个 jail 必须先于另一个 jail 运行，请在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中使用 `depend` 参数表达这种关系，而不要依赖列表顺序。每个 jail 的依赖项都会在其启动前自动创建，并按相反顺序停止，无论 `jail_list` 如何排列。`depend` 参数的说明见 crossref:jails[jail-configuration-files,Jail 配置文件]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:256
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Networking"
msgstr "网络"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:259
#, fuzzy
msgid "Networking for FreeBSD jails can be configured several different ways:"
msgstr "FreeBSD jail 的网络可以通过多种方式配置："

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:260
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Host Networking Mode (IP Sharing)"
msgstr "宿主网络模式（共享 IP）"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:264
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In host networking mode a jail shares the host's network stack instead of "
"receiving its own.  Sharing the stack does not mean sharing the address: the "
"common setup gives the jail its own dedicated `ip4.addr` (and `ip6.addr`) "
"that man:jail[8] adds as an alias on the host interface, so the jail and the "
"host answer on different addresses over the same stack.  Only a jail "
"configured with `ip4 = inherit` shares the host's addresses wholesale and "
"answers on the host's own address, gaining unrestricted access to every "
"address the host holds."
msgstr "在宿主网络模式下，jail 共享宿主系统的网络协议栈，而不是获得自己的协议栈。共享协议栈并不意味着共享地址：常见配置会为 jail 指定专用的 `ip4.addr`（以及 `ip6.addr`），由 man:jail[8] 将其作为宿主接口的别名添加，因此 jail 和宿主系统会通过同一协议栈在不同地址上响应。只有配置了 `ip4 = inherit` 的 jail 才会完整继承宿主系统的地址，并以宿主系统自己的地址响应，从而能够不受限制地访问宿主系统持有的所有地址。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:265
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Virtual Networks (VNET)"
msgstr "虚拟网络（VNET）"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:269
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Virtual Networks are a feature of FreeBSD jails that offer more advanced and "
"flexible networking solutions than a basic networking mode like host "
"networking.  VNET allows the creation of isolated network stacks for each "
"jail, providing them with their own separate IP addresses, routing tables, "
"and network interfaces.  This offers a higher level of network isolation and "
"allows jails to function as if they are running on separate virtual machines."
msgstr "虚拟网络是 FreeBSD jail 的一项功能，与宿主网络等基本网络模式相比，可提供更高级、更灵活的网络解决方案。VNET 可为每个 jail 创建隔离的网络协议栈，使其拥有独立的 IP 地址、路由表和网络接口。这样可以提供更高级别的网络隔离，并使 jail 能够像在独立虚拟机中运行一样工作。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:270
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "The netgraph system"
msgstr "netgraph 系统"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:273
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:netgraph[4] is a versatile kernel framework for creating custom network "
"configurations.  It can be used to define how network traffic flows between "
"jails and the host system and between different jails."
msgstr "man:netgraph[4] 是一个功能强大的内核框架，可用于创建自定义网络配置。它可用于定义网络流量如何在 jail 与主机系统之间以及不同 jail 之间流动。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:275
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Where a Jail's IP Address Comes From"
msgstr "Jail 的 IP 地址从何而来"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:280
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A shared-stack jail reaches the network through an address on a host "
"interface.  The `interface` parameter names that interface, and for every "
"address in `ip4.addr` and `ip6.addr` man:jail[8] manages the alias itself: "
"as jail(8) puts it, \"an alias for each address will be added to the "
"interface before the jail is created, and will be removed from the interface "
"after the jail is removed\".  Nothing on the host has to pre-configure the "
"address."
msgstr "共享协议栈的 jail 通过主机接口上的地址访问网络。`interface` 参数指定该接口；对于 `ip4.addr` 和 `ip6.addr` 中的每个地址，man:jail[8] 都会自行管理别名：正如 jail(8) 所述：“创建 jail 之前，会将每个地址作为别名添加到接口；移除 jail 之后，会从接口中删除该别名”。主机无需预先配置该地址。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:282
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The interface can also be given per address, so a single line ties an "
"address to the interface that should carry it:"
msgstr "也可以为每个地址单独指定接口，这样一行配置就能将地址与承载它的接口关联起来："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:286
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ip4.addr = \"em0|192.168.1.151/24\";\n"
msgstr "ip4.addr = \"em0|192.168.1.151/24\";\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:289
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When an address must persist independently of the jail — because another "
"service on the host relies on it, or because the `interface` parameter is "
"not used — assign it on the host as an rc.conf alias and leave it out of "
"jail(8)'s management:"
msgstr "如果地址必须独立于 jail 持续存在——例如主机上的其他服务依赖该地址，或未使用 `interface` 参数——请在主机上将其配置为 rc.conf 别名，并避免将其交由 jail(8) 管理："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:293
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sysrc ifconfig_em0_aliases=\"inet 192.168.1.151/32\"\n"
msgstr "# sysrc ifconfig_em0_aliases=\"inet 192.168.1.151/32\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:296
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The older, numbered form `ifconfig_em0_alias0=\"inet 192.168.1.151/32\"` "
"still works, but the `_aliases` form is preferred for new configurations "
"because it avoids the fragile requirement that the numbered aliases form an "
"unbroken `alias0`, `alias1`, `alias2` sequence."
msgstr "较旧的编号形式 `ifconfig_em0_alias0=\"inet 192.168.1.151/32\"` 仍然有效，但新配置更推荐使用 `_aliases` 形式，因为它不需要编号别名必须按 `alias0`、`alias1`、`alias2` 连续排列这一脆弱条件。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:298
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Loopback Addresses in Shared-IP Jails"
msgstr "共享 IP Jail 中的环回地址"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:303
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A shared-stack jail has no loopback interface of its own.  The FreeBSD "
"kernel compensates for this: in a non-VNET jail, whenever `127.0.0.1` or "
"`::1` is not itself one of the jail's own addresses, the kernel silently "
"rewrites both `bind()` and `connect()` on the loopback address to the jail's "
"first `ip4.addr` or `ip6.addr`.  This behavior is not documented in man:"
"jail[8], but it matters, because it carries a security consequence."
msgstr "共享协议栈的 jail 没有自己的环回接口。FreeBSD 内核会对此进行补偿：在非 VNET jail 中，只要 `127.0.0.1` 或 `::1` 不是 jail 自身的地址之一，内核就会静默地将针对环回地址的 `bind()` 和 `connect()` 都重写为 jail 的第一个 `ip4.addr` 或 `ip6.addr`。man:jail[8] 并未记录此行为，但它很重要，因为这会带来安全影响。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:308
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Do not assume that binding a service to `localhost` confines it to the "
"jail.  In a shared-IP jail a daemon told to listen on `127.0.0.1` actually "
"binds the jail's first address, which is frequently a LAN-facing one, and so "
"becomes reachable from the network."
msgstr "不要认为将服务绑定到 `localhost` 就能将其限制在 jail 内。在共享 IP jail 中，如果要求守护进程监听 `127.0.0.1`，它实际上会绑定到 jail 的第一个地址；该地址通常面向局域网，因此该服务也会从网络上可访问。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:312
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The standard mitigation is to give the jail a private loopback address and "
"list it first.  Clone a dedicated loopback interface on the host and assign "
"it an address in the `127.0.0.0/8` range (or a private RFC 1918 address):"
msgstr "标准的缓解措施是为 jail 配置一个专用环回地址，并将其列在首位。在主机上克隆一个专用环回接口，并为其分配 `127.0.0.0/8` 范围内的地址（或 RFC 1918 私有地址）："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:317
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# sysrc cloned_interfaces=\"lo1\"\n"
"# sysrc ifconfig_lo1=\"inet 127.0.1.1/32\"\n"
msgstr "# sysrc cloned_interfaces=\"lo1\"\n# sysrc ifconfig_lo1=\"inet 127.0.1.1/32\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:320
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then list that address first in the jail's `ip4.addr`, ahead of any routable "
"address, so the loopback remap lands on the private address instead of a LAN-"
"facing one."
msgstr "然后将该地址列在 jail 的 `ip4.addr` 首位，放在任何可路由地址之前，这样环回地址重映射就会指向私有地址，而不是面向局域网的地址。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:322
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Preparing Host Services"
msgstr "准备主机服务"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:327
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Each jail alias address shares the host's ports.  A host daemon bound to the "
"wildcard address — shown as `*:port` in listener listings — is therefore "
"listening on every jail alias too, and it occupies that port before a jail's "
"own service can claim it.  Before starting any jails, audit what the host "
"already listens on:"
msgstr "每个 jail 别名地址都与主机共用端口。因此，绑定到通配地址的主机守护进程——在监听器列表中显示为 `*:port`——也会监听所有 jail 别名，并且会先占用该端口，使 jail 自己的服务无法使用。启动任何 jail 之前，请检查主机当前的监听情况："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:331
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sockstat -4 -6 -l\n"
msgstr "# sockstat -4 -6 -l\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:334
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Restrict each daemon that binds a wildcard address so it uses only the "
"host's own address and leaves the jail addresses free:"
msgstr "限制每个绑定到通配地址的守护进程，使其仅使用主机自身的地址，从而为 jail 地址留出空间："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:337
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:syslogd[8]: set `syslogd_flags=\"-ss\"` in [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#.  A "
"single `-s` already runs syslogd in secure mode so it does not listen for "
"remote log messages; per syslogd(8), if `-s` \"is specified twice, no "
"network socket will be opened at all\", which also stops syslogd from "
"sending to remote hosts."
msgstr "man:syslogd[8]：在 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中设置 `syslogd_flags=\"-ss\"`。单个 `-s` 已会让 syslogd 进入安全模式，不再监听远程日志消息；根据 syslogd(8) 的说明，如果“`-s` 被指定两次，则完全不会打开网络套接字”，这也会阻止 syslogd 向远程主机发送消息。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:338
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:sshd[8]: pin `ListenAddress` to the host's address in [.filename]#/etc/"
"ssh/sshd_config# instead of leaving it on the default wildcard."
msgstr "man:sshd[8]：在 [.filename]#/etc/ssh/sshd_config# 中将 `ListenAddress` 固定为主机地址，而不要使用默认的通配地址。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:339
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:ntpd[8] and man:sendmail[8]: bind them to the host address as well "
"through their own configuration."
msgstr "man:ntpd[8] 和 man:sendmail[8]：也应通过各自的配置将它们绑定到主机地址。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:341
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For firewall-level control over which addresses a jail may use, see crossref:"
"firewalls[firewalls,Firewalls]."
msgstr "如需在防火墙层面控制 jail 可以使用哪些地址，请参阅 crossref:firewalls[firewalls,防火墙]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:343
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Setting Up the Jail Directory Tree"
msgstr "设置 Jail 目录树"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:346
#, fuzzy
msgid "There is no specific place to put the files for the jails."
msgstr "Jail 文件没有特定的存放位置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:349
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Some administrators use [.filename]#/jail#, others [.filename]#/usr/jail#, "
"and still others [.filename]#/usr/local/jails#.  In this chapter [."
"filename]#/usr/local/jails# will be used."
msgstr "有些管理员使用 [.filename]#/jail#，有些使用 [.filename]#/usr/jail#，还有些使用 [.filename]#/usr/local/jails#。本章将使用 [.filename]#/usr/local/jails#。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:351
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Apart from [.filename]#/usr/local/jails# other directories will be created:"
msgstr "除 [.filename]#/usr/local/jails# 外，还将创建其他目录："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:353
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#media# will contain the compressed files of the downloaded "
"userlands."
msgstr "[.filename]#media# 用于存放已下载用户空间的压缩文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:354
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#templates# will contain the templates when using Thin Jails."
msgstr "使用 Thin Jail 时，[.filename]#templates# 用于存放模板。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:355
#, fuzzy
msgid "[.filename]#containers# will contain the jails."
msgstr "[.filename]#containers# 用于存放 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:357
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When using OpenZFS, execute the following commands to create datasets for "
"these directories:"
msgstr "使用 OpenZFS 时，执行以下命令为这些目录创建数据集："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:364
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zfs create -o mountpoint=/usr/local/jails zroot/jails\n"
"# zfs create zroot/jails/media\n"
"# zfs create zroot/jails/templates\n"
"# zfs create zroot/jails/containers\n"
msgstr "# zfs create -o mountpoint=/usr/local/jails zroot/jails\n# zfs create zroot/jails/media\n# zfs create zroot/jails/templates\n# zfs create zroot/jails/containers\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:369
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In this case, `zroot` was used for the parent dataset, but other datasets "
"could have been used."
msgstr "此处使用了 `zroot` 作为父数据集，但也可以使用其他数据集。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:373
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Creating a separate child dataset per jail is what later enables per-jail "
"snapshots, clones, quotas, and dataset delegation.  Because each jail "
"directory is then its own dataset, OpenZFS can both cap and guarantee its "
"disk use with the `quota` and `reservation` properties; see crossref:"
"jails[jail-resource-limits,Jail Resource Limits]."
msgstr "为每个 jail 单独创建子数据集，之后便可对其进行快照、克隆、配额管理和数据集委派。由于每个 jail 目录都是独立的数据集，OpenZFS 可以通过 `quota` 和 `reservation` 属性限制并保障其磁盘空间使用量；请参阅 crossref:jails[jail-resource-limits,Jail 资源限制]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:375
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When using UFS, execute the following commands to create the directories:"
msgstr "使用 UFS 时，执行以下命令创建目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:382
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mkdir /usr/local/jails/\n"
"# mkdir /usr/local/jails/media\n"
"# mkdir /usr/local/jails/templates\n"
"# mkdir /usr/local/jails/containers\n"
msgstr "# mkdir /usr/local/jails/\n# mkdir /usr/local/jails/media\n# mkdir /usr/local/jails/templates\n# mkdir /usr/local/jails/containers\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:385
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Time Zone Configuration"
msgid "Jail Configuration Files"
msgstr "设置时区"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:388
#, fuzzy
msgid "There are two ways to configure jails."
msgstr "配置 jail 有两种方法。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:391
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first one is to add an entry for each jail to the file [.filename]#/etc/"
"jail.conf#.  The other option is to create a file for each jail in the "
"directory [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/#."
msgstr "第一种是在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 文件中为每个 jail 添加一条配置。另一种方法是在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/# 目录中为每个 jail 创建一个文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:394
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In case a host system has few jails, an entry for each jail can be added in "
"the file [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#.  If the host system has many jails, it "
"is a good idea to have one configuration file for each jail in the [."
"filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/# directory."
msgstr "如果主机系统上的 jail 数量较少，可以在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 文件中为每个 jail 添加一条配置。如果主机系统上有许多 jail，则建议在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/# 目录中为每个 jail 单独创建一个配置文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:396
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The files in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/# must have `.conf` as their "
"extension and have to be included in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#:"
msgstr "[.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d/# 中的文件必须使用 `.conf` 扩展名，并且必须在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中包含："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:400
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ".include \"/etc/jail.conf.d/*.conf\";\n"
msgstr ".include \"/etc/jail.conf.d/*.conf\";\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:403
#, fuzzy
msgid "A typical jail entry would look like this:"
msgstr "典型的 jail 配置如下："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:411
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"jailname { <.>\n"
"  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n"
"  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\"; <.>\n"
"  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\"; <.>\n"
"  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\"; <.>\n"
msgstr "jailname { <.>\n  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\"; <.>\n  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\"; <.>\n  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\"; <.>\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:416
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # PERMISSIONS\n"
"  allow.raw_sockets; <.>\n"
"  exec.clean; <.>\n"
"  mount.devfs; <.>\n"
msgstr "  # PERMISSIONS\n  allow.raw_sockets; <.>\n  exec.clean; <.>\n  mount.devfs; <.>\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:420
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # HOSTNAME/PATH\n"
"  host.hostname = \"${name}\"; <.>\n"
"  path = \"/usr/local/jails/containers/${name}\"; <.>\n"
msgstr "  # HOSTNAME/PATH\n  host.hostname = \"${name}\"; <.>\n  path = \"/usr/local/jails/containers/${name}\"; <.>\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:426
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # NETWORK\n"
"  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.151; <.>\n"
"  ip6.addr = \"2001:db8::151\"; <.>\n"
"  interface = em0; <.>\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "  # NETWORK\n  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.151; <.>\n  ip6.addr = \"2001:db8::151\"; <.>\n  interface = em0; <.>\n}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:429
#, fuzzy
msgid "`jailname` - Name of the jail."
msgstr "`jailname` - Jail 的名称。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:431
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`exec.start` - Command(s) to run in the jail environment when a jail is "
"created.  A typical command to run is \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\"."
msgstr "`exec.start` - 创建 jail 时在 jail 环境中运行的命令。典型命令为 \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\"。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:433
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`exec.stop` - Command(s) to run in the jail environment before a jail is "
"removed.  A typical command to run is \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\"."
msgstr "`exec.stop` - 移除 jail 前在 jail 环境中运行的命令。典型命令为 \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\"。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:434
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`exec.consolelog` - A file to direct command output (stdout and stderr) to."
msgstr "`exec.consolelog` - 用于接收命令输出（标准输出和标准错误）的文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:436
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`allow.raw_sockets` - Allow creating raw sockets inside the jail.  Setting "
"this parameter allows utilities like man:ping[8] and man:traceroute[8] to "
"operate inside the jail."
msgstr "`allow.raw_sockets` - 允许在 jail 内创建原始套接字。设置此参数后，man:ping[8] 和 man:traceroute[8] 等实用工具便可在 jail 内运行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:437
#, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.clean` - Run commands in a clean environment."
msgstr "`exec.clean` - 在干净的环境中运行命令。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:439
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`mount.devfs` - Mount a man:devfs[5] filesystem on the chrooted [.filename]#/"
"dev# directory to restrict the devices visible inside the jail.  It applies "
"the ruleset named by the `devfs_ruleset` parameter, or, when that parameter "
"is left at its default of `0`, the `mount.devfs` fallback of ruleset 4, "
"`devfsrules_jail`, which hides every host device except a minimal, jail-safe "
"set (see crossref:jails[jail-conf-devfs, Devfs Rulesets])."
msgstr "`mount.devfs` - 在 chroot 后的 [.filename]#/dev# 目录上挂载 man:devfs[5] 文件系统，以限制 jail 内可见的设备。此参数使用 `devfs_ruleset` 参数指定的规则集；如果该参数保留默认值 `0`，则 `mount.devfs` 会回退到规则集 4 `devfsrules_jail`，该规则集会隐藏所有主机设备，仅保留最基本且适用于 jail 的设备集（请参阅 crossref:jails[jail-conf-devfs,Devfs 规则集]）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:440
#, fuzzy
msgid "`host.hostname` - The hostname of the jail."
msgstr "`host.hostname` - Jail 的主机名。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:442
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`path` - The directory which is to be the root of the jail.  Any commands "
"that are run inside the jail, either by jail or from man:jexec[8], are run "
"from this directory."
msgstr "`path` - 作为 jail 根目录的目录。通过 jail 或 man:jexec[8] 在 jail 内运行的所有命令，都会从此目录运行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:447
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`ip4.addr` - One IPv4 address, or a comma-separated list of addresses, "
"assigned to the jail.  Setting `ip4.addr` implies `ip4 = new`; `ip4` itself "
"is not left at a standalone default.  The `ip4` parameter accepts three "
"values: `new` restricts the jail to the addresses listed in `ip4.addr`, "
"`inherit` gives the jail unrestricted access to every IPv4 address of the "
"host, and `disable` turns off IPv4 in the jail entirely.  A jail with "
"neither `ip4` nor `ip4.addr` set behaves like `inherit`, and `interface` and "
"`ip4.addr` have no effect under `inherit`.  In a jail with several "
"addresses, `ip4.saddrsel` lets the kernel choose the source address for "
"outgoing connections on unbound sockets, while `ip4.nosaddrsel` forces the "
"first address in the list."
msgstr "`ip4.addr` - 分配给 jail 的一个 IPv4 地址或以逗号分隔的地址列表。设置 `ip4.addr` 会隐含设置 `ip4 = new`；`ip4` 本身不会保持为独立的默认值。`ip4` 参数接受三个值：`new` 将 jail 限制为 `ip4.addr` 中列出的地址；`inherit` 允许 jail 不受限制地访问主机的所有 IPv4 地址；`disable` 则完全关闭 jail 中的 IPv4。若既未设置 `ip4`，也未设置 `ip4.addr`，则 jail 的行为与 `inherit` 相同；在 `inherit` 模式下，`interface` 和 `ip4.addr` 均不起作用。对于具有多个地址的 jail，`ip4.saddrsel` 允许内核为未绑定套接字上的外发连接选择源地址，而 `ip4.nosaddrsel` 则强制使用列表中的第一个地址。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:450
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`ip6.addr` - One IPv6 address, or a comma-separated list of addresses, "
"assigned to the jail.  The `ip6` parameter takes the same `new`, `inherit`, "
"and `disable` values as `ip4`, with `ip6.saddrsel` and `ip6.nosaddrsel` "
"controlling source-address selection.  Use `ip6 = disable` for an IPv4-only "
"jail, or `ip4 = disable` for an IPv6-only one."
msgstr "`ip6.addr` - 分配给 jail 的一个 IPv6 地址或以逗号分隔的地址列表。`ip6` 参数与 `ip4` 一样接受 `new`、`inherit` 和 `disable`，并可通过 `ip6.saddrsel` 和 `ip6.nosaddrsel` 控制源地址选择。仅使用 IPv4 的 jail 可设置 `ip6 = disable`；仅使用 IPv6 的 jail 可设置 `ip4 = disable`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:452
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`interface` - A network interface to add the jail's IP addresses.  Usually "
"the host interface."
msgstr "`interface` - 用于添加 jail IP 地址的网络接口，通常是主机接口。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:459
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A jail has no virtual console: man:init[8] and man:getty[8] do not run "
"inside it, so there is nothing to attach to interactively.  The `exec."
"consolelog` file captures only the standard output and standard error of the "
"`exec.*` commands, that is, the output of the [.filename]#/etc/rc# startup "
"and [.filename]#/etc/rc.shutdown# scripts.  It is not an interactive "
"console; for that, use man:jexec[8] (see crossref:jails[access-jail, Access "
"a Jail]) or run man:sshd[8] inside the jail.  The jail's own daemons send "
"their later output to the jail's syslog."
msgstr "Jail 没有虚拟控制台：man:init[8] 和 man:getty[8] 不会在 jail 内运行，因此没有可供交互连接的对象。`exec.consolelog` 文件只会捕获 `exec.*` 命令的标准输出和标准错误，也就是 [.filename]#/etc/rc# 启动脚本和 [.filename]#/etc/rc.shutdown# 脚本的输出。它不是交互式控制台；如需交互，请使用 man:jexec[8]（请参阅 crossref:jails[access-jail,访问 Jail]），或在 jail 内运行 man:sshd[8]。Jail 自身守护进程之后产生的输出会发送到 jail 的 syslog。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:465
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `exec.consolelog` files grow without bound.  Rotate them with man:"
"newsyslog[8] by adding a single glob entry, for example in [.filename]#/etc/"
"newsyslog.conf.d/jail#:"
msgstr "`exec.consolelog` 文件会不断增大。可通过 man:newsyslog[8] 轮转这些文件，例如在 [.filename]#/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/jail# 中添加一条通配规则："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:469
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "/var/log/jail_console_*.log            640  7     100  *     J\n"
msgstr "/var/log/jail_console_*.log            640  7     100  *     J\n"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:473
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Global Settings, Wildcards and Variables"
msgstr "全局设置、通配符和变量"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:477
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Parameters set outside any jail block are wildcard defaults: man:jail."
"conf[5] applies them to every jail, exactly as if they were written in a `*` "
"wildcard section.  Setting the shared parameters once keeps each jail block "
"short."
msgstr "在任何 jail 配置块之外设置的参数都是通配默认值：man:jail.conf[5] 会将它们应用于每个 jail，效果与将这些参数写在 `*` 通配符区段中完全相同。一次性设置共享参数可使每个 jail 配置块更简洁。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:480
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A name preceded by a dollar sign, and optionally enclosed in braces, is "
"replaced with the value of that parameter or variable.  The built-in `${name}"
"` expands to the jail's own name, and a custom variable is defined just like "
"a parameter but with a leading dollar sign."
msgstr "前面带美元符号且可选地用花括号括起来的名称，会替换为对应参数或变量的值。内置变量 `${name}` 会展开为 jail 自身的名称；自定义变量的定义方式与参数相同，但名称前要加美元符号。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:482
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# defines a common header once and "
"overrides only what differs per jail:"
msgstr "以下 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 配置只定义一次通用配置头，并且仅覆盖各 jail 之间不同的部分："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:494
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# Shared defaults applied to every jail\n"
"exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n"
"exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n"
"exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"
"exec.clean;\n"
"mount.devfs;\n"
"host.hostname = \"${name}\";\n"
"path = \"/usr/local/jails/containers/${name}\";\n"
"interface = em0;\n"
msgstr "# Shared defaults applied to every jail\nexec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\nexec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\nexec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\nexec.clean;\nmount.devfs;\nhost.hostname = \"${name}\";\npath = \"/usr/local/jails/containers/${name}\";\ninterface = em0;\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:498
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"www {\n"
"    ip4.addr = 192.168.1.151;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "www {\n    ip4.addr = 192.168.1.151;\n}\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:503
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"db {\n"
"    host.hostname = \"database.example.com\";\n"
"    ip4.addr = 192.168.1.152;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "db {\n    host.hostname = \"database.example.com\";\n    ip4.addr = 192.168.1.152;\n}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:506
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Here `www` inherits everything from the header and sets only its address, "
"while `db` also overrides `host.hostname`."
msgstr "这里，`www` 继承配置头中的所有设置，只设置自己的地址；而 `db` 还覆盖了 `host.hostname`。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:508
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Command Hooks"
msgstr "命令钩子"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:512
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:jail[8] runs a jail through a sequence of lifecycle hooks, and it "
"matters whether each one runs in the host environment or inside the jail.  "
"In creation order:"
msgstr "man:jail[8] 通过一系列生命周期钩子来运行 jail；每个钩子是在主机环境中运行还是在 jail 内运行，都很重要。按创建顺序如下："

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:513
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.prestart`"
msgstr "`exec.prestart`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:514
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runs in the host environment before the jail is created."
msgstr "在创建 jail 之前于主机环境中运行。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:514
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.created`"
msgstr "`exec.created`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:515
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Runs in the host environment after the jail exists but before any process "
"starts inside it."
msgstr "在 jail 创建之后、其中任何进程启动之前于主机环境中运行。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:515
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.start`"
msgstr "`exec.start`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:516
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Runs inside the jail, typically `/bin/sh /etc/rc` to bring up its services."
msgstr "在 jail 内运行，通常执行 `/bin/sh /etc/rc` 来启动其服务。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:516
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.poststart`"
msgstr "`exec.poststart`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:517
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runs in the host environment after the jail has started."
msgstr "在 jail 启动之后于主机环境中运行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:519
#, fuzzy
msgid "Shutdown runs the mirror image:"
msgstr "关闭过程按相反顺序进行："

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:520
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.prestop`"
msgstr "`exec.prestop`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:521
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runs in the host environment before the jail is stopped."
msgstr "在停止 jail 之前于主机环境中运行。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:521
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.stop`"
msgstr "`exec.stop`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:522
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runs inside the jail, typically `/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown`."
msgstr "在 jail 内运行，通常为 `/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown`。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:522
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`exec.poststop`"
msgstr "`exec.poststop`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:523
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Runs in the host environment after the jail has stopped, to tear down "
"whatever `exec.prestart` set up."
msgstr "在 jail 停止后于主机环境中运行，用于拆除 `exec.prestart` 所设置的内容。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:525
#, fuzzy
msgid "A hook may be assigned more than one command by appending with `+=`:"
msgstr "可以通过追加 `+=` 为钩子指定多个命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:529
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "exec.poststart += \"logger jail ${name} started\";\n"
msgstr "exec.poststart += \"logger jail ${name} started\";\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:533
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`exec.timeout` caps how long man:jail[8] waits for a command to finish, and "
"`exec.consolelog` captures the output of these commands.  The VNET section "
"(crossref:jails[creating-vnet-jail, VNET Jails]) uses `exec.prestart` and "
"`exec.poststop` to build and tear down each jail's network plumbing on the "
"host."
msgstr "`exec.timeout` 限制 man:jail[8] 等待命令完成的时间，`exec.consolelog` 则会捕获这些命令的输出。VNET 一节（crossref:jails[creating-vnet-jail, VNET Jails]）使用 `exec.prestart` 和 `exec.poststop` 在主机上为每个 jail 创建和拆除网络配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:536
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Where hooks order commands within a single jail, the `depend` parameter "
"orders whole jails.  Writing `depend = otherjail;` tells man:jail[8] that "
"this jail requires `otherjail`: the dependency is created first, up to the "
"completion of its last `exec.poststart` command, before this jail is "
"created, and the jails are torn down in the reverse order."
msgstr "钩子用于安排单个 jail 内命令的顺序，而 `depend` 参数用于安排整个 jail 的顺序。写入 `depend = otherjail;` 会告知 man:jail[8] 此 jail 依赖于 `otherjail`：创建此 jail 之前会先创建依赖项，并等待其最后一个 `exec.poststart` 命令完成；拆除 jail 时则按相反顺序进行。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:538
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Devfs Rulesets"
msgstr "Devfs 规则集"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:544
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Every jail that sets `mount.devfs` gets a devfs ruleset that decides which "
"device nodes appear under its [.filename]#/dev#, either the one named by the "
"`devfs_ruleset` parameter or, when that parameter is unset, the `mount."
"devfs` default of ruleset 4.  man:devfs.rules[5] defines named rulesets in [."
"filename]#/etc/defaults/devfs.rules#.  Two of them are meant for jails: "
"`devfsrules_jail`, ruleset 4, is the standard minimal device set for a jail, "
"and `devfsrules_jail_vnet`, ruleset 5, adds [.filename]#/dev/pf# so a VNET "
"jail can run its own firewall.  The VNET jail examples set `devfs_ruleset = "
"5` and the Linux jail example sets `devfs_ruleset = 4`; the classic and thin-"
"jail examples set only `mount.devfs` and so use its default of ruleset 4."
msgstr "每个设置了 `mount.devfs` 的 jail 都会获得一个 devfs 规则集，用于决定其 [.filename]#/dev# 下显示哪些设备节点。规则集可以由 `devfs_ruleset` 参数指定；如果未设置该参数，则使用 `mount.devfs` 默认的规则集 4。man:devfs.rules[5] 在 [.filename]#/etc/defaults/devfs.rules# 中定义命名规则集。其中两个规则集专供 jail 使用：`devfsrules_jail`（规则集 4）是 jail 的标准最小设备集；`devfsrules_jail_vnet`（规则集 5）则额外包含 [.filename]#/dev/pf#，使 VNET jail 能运行自己的防火墙。VNET jail 示例设置 `devfs_ruleset = 5`，Linux jail 示例设置 `devfs_ruleset = 4`；经典 jail 和薄型 jail 示例只设置 `mount.devfs`，因此使用其默认规则集 4。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:547
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To expose an extra device, write a custom ruleset in [.filename]#/etc/devfs."
"rules# that includes one of the stock rulesets and unhides what it needs.  "
"The following ruleset starts from `devfsrules_jail` and additionally unhides "
"the man:bpf[4] devices:"
msgstr "要公开额外设备，请在 [.filename]#/etc/devfs.rules# 中编写自定义规则集，其中包含一个内置规则集，并取消隐藏所需设备。以下规则集以 `devfsrules_jail` 为基础，另外取消隐藏 man:bpf[4] 设备："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:553
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[devfsrules_jail_bpf=100]\n"
"add include $devfsrules_jail\n"
"add path 'bpf*' unhide\n"
msgstr "[devfsrules_jail_bpf=100]\nadd include $devfsrules_jail\nadd path 'bpf*' unhide\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:556
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Reload the rules, then reference the new ruleset by its number in the jail's "
"configuration:"
msgstr "重新加载规则，然后在 jail 配置中通过编号引用新规则集："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:560
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service devfs restart\n"
msgstr "# service devfs restart\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:565
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "devfs_ruleset = 100;\n"
msgstr "devfs_ruleset = 100;\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:568
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rulesets in [.filename]#/etc/devfs.rules# override same-numbered rulesets in "
"[.filename]#/etc/defaults/devfs.rules#; otherwise the two files are "
"effectively merged."
msgstr "[.filename]#/etc/devfs.rules# 中的规则集会覆盖 [.filename]#/etc/defaults/devfs.rules# 中编号相同的规则集；否则，这两个文件实际上会合并。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:570
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"More information about configuration variables can be found in man:jail[8] "
"and man:jail.conf[5]."
msgstr "有关配置变量的更多信息，请参阅 man:jail[8] 和 man:jail.conf[5]。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:572
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Classic Jail (Thick Jail)"
msgstr "经典 jail（厚型 jail）"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:576
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These jails resemble a real FreeBSD system.  They can be managed more or "
"less like a normal host system and updated independently."
msgstr "这类 jail 类似于真实的 FreeBSD 系统。它们的管理方式与普通主机系统大致相同，并且可以独立更新。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:578
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Creating and Controlling Jails"
msgid "Creating a Classic Jail"
msgstr "创建和控制 Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:581
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In principle, a jail only needs a hostname, a root directory, an IP address, "
"and a userland."
msgstr "原则上，jail 只需要主机名、根目录、IP 地址和用户空间。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:583
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The userland for the jail can be obtained from the official FreeBSD download "
"servers."
msgstr "可以从 FreeBSD 官方下载服务器获取 jail 的用户空间。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:585
#, fuzzy
msgid "Execute the following command to download the userland:"
msgstr "执行以下命令下载用户空间："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:589
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:795
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:899
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# fetch https://download.freebsd.org/releases/amd64/amd64/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/base.txz -o /usr/local/jails/media/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base.txz\n"
msgstr "# fetch https://download.freebsd.org/releases/amd64/amd64/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/base.txz -o /usr/local/jails/media/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base.txz\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:592
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Once the command is complete, the next step is configuring the host to "
#| "run the jail."
msgid ""
"Once the download is complete, it will be necessary to extract the contents "
"into the jail directory."
msgstr "命令完成后，下一步来配置主机以运行 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:594
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Execute the following commands to extract the userland into the jail's "
"directory:"
msgstr "执行以下命令，将用户空间解压到 jail 目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:599
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mkdir -p /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"
"# tar -xf /usr/local/jails/media/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base.txz -C /usr/local/jails/containers/classic --unlink\n"
msgstr "# mkdir -p /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n# tar -xf /usr/local/jails/media/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base.txz -C /usr/local/jails/containers/classic --unlink\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:602
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the userland extracted in the jail directory, it will be necessary to "
"copy the timezone and DNS server files:"
msgstr "将用户空间解压到 jail 目录后，需要复制时区和 DNS 服务器文件："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:607
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cp /etc/resolv.conf /usr/local/jails/containers/classic/etc/resolv.conf\n"
"# cp /etc/localtime /usr/local/jails/containers/classic/etc/localtime\n"
msgstr "# cp /etc/resolv.conf /usr/local/jails/containers/classic/etc/resolv.conf\n# cp /etc/localtime /usr/local/jails/containers/classic/etc/localtime\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:610
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the files copied, the next thing to do is update to the latest patch "
"level by executing the following command:"
msgstr "复制文件后，接下来需要执行以下命令，将系统更新到最新补丁级别："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:614
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/containers/classic/ fetch install\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/containers/classic/ fetch install\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:618
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:839
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The last step is to configure the jail.  It will be necessary to add an "
"entry to the configuration file [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# or in [."
"filename]#jail.conf.d# with the parameters of the jail."
msgstr "最后一步是配置 jail。需要将 jail 的参数添加到配置文件 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 或 [.filename]#jail.conf.d# 中。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:620
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:841
#, fuzzy
msgid "An example would be the following:"
msgstr "例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:628
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"classic {\n"
"  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n"
"  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n"
"  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n"
"  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"
msgstr "classic {\n  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:633
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:748
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:854
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1008
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # PERMISSIONS\n"
"  allow.raw_sockets;\n"
"  exec.clean;\n"
"  mount.devfs;\n"
msgstr "  # PERMISSIONS\n  allow.raw_sockets;\n  exec.clean;\n  mount.devfs;\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:637
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:752
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:858
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1316
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # HOSTNAME/PATH\n"
"  host.hostname = \"${name}\";\n"
"  path = \"/usr/local/jails/containers/${name}\";\n"
msgstr "  # HOSTNAME/PATH\n  host.hostname = \"${name}\";\n  path = \"/usr/local/jails/containers/${name}\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:642
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # NETWORK\n"
"  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.151;\n"
"  interface = em0;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "  # NETWORK\n  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.151;\n  interface = em0;\n}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:645
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:866
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1036
#, fuzzy
msgid "Execute the following command to start the jail:"
msgstr "执行以下命令启动 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:649
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service jail start classic\n"
msgstr "# service jail start classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:652
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:874
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"More information on how to manage jails can be found in the section crossref:"
"jails[jail-management, Jail Management]."
msgstr "有关如何管理 jail 的更多信息，请参阅 crossref:jails[jail-management, Jail Management] 一节。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:654
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Obtaining the Jail Userland"
msgstr "获取 jail 用户空间"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:658
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fetch-and-extract procedure shown above is the traditional way to "
"populate a jail's root directory, but it is not the only one.  The same "
"userland can be installed with man:bsdinstall[8], from base-system packages, "
"or from a locally built source tree."
msgstr "上文所示的获取并解压流程是填充 jail 根目录的传统方法，但并非唯一方法。也可以使用 man:bsdinstall[8]、基础系统软件包或本地构建的源代码树来安装相同的用户空间。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:661
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:bsdinstall[8] provides a dedicated `jail` target that sets up a new "
"userland at the given directory for use with man:jail[8].  It fetches and "
"extracts the distribution sets without installing a kernel, skipping the "
"disk partitioning and network steps of a normal installation, which makes it "
"a one-command, scriptable alternative to the manual fetch and man:tar[1] "
"sequence:"
msgstr "man:bsdinstall[8] 提供专用的 `jail` 目标，可在指定目录中设置新的用户空间，以供 man:jail[8] 使用。它会获取并解压发行版集合，而不会安装内核；同时跳过常规安装中的磁盘分区和网络步骤，因此可通过一条命令完成，也便于编写脚本，是手动执行 fetch 和 man:tar[1] 操作的替代方案："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:665
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# bsdinstall jail /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# bsdinstall jail /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:669
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `jail` target installs the base distribution ([.filename]#base.txz#) by "
"default.  On FreeBSD 15.0 and later man:bsdinstall[8] can also populate the "
"root from base-system packages with its `pkgbase` target; the pkg-based "
"method is described next."
msgstr "`jail` 目标默认安装基本发行版（[.filename]#base.txz#）。从 FreeBSD 15.0 开始，man:bsdinstall[8] 还可以通过 `pkgbase` 目标使用基础系统软件包填充根目录；基于软件包的方法将在下文介绍。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:672
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Starting with FreeBSD 15.0 the base system is also published as packages, so "
"a jail userland can be installed entirely with man:pkg[8] from the `FreeBSD-"
"base` repository.  Point man:pkg[8] at the jail's root directory with the "
"global `--rootdir` option and install the jail variant of the base set:"
msgstr "从 FreeBSD 15.0 开始，基础系统也以软件包形式发布，因此可以完全通过 man:pkg[8] 从 `FreeBSD-base` 仓库安装 jail 用户空间。使用全局 `--rootdir` 选项将 man:pkg[8] 指向 jail 的根目录，并安装 jail 版的基础集合："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:676
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# pkg --rootdir /usr/local/jails/containers/classic install -r FreeBSD-base FreeBSD-set-base-jail\n"
msgstr "# pkg --rootdir /usr/local/jails/containers/classic install -r FreeBSD-base FreeBSD-set-base-jail\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:680
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use `FreeBSD-set-minimal-jail` instead of `FreeBSD-set-base-jail` for a "
"minimal userland.  A jail installed this way is afterwards patched and "
"upgraded with man:pkg[8] rather than man:freebsd-update[8]; see crossref:"
"jails[jail-upgrade-pkgbase, Upgrading pkgbase Jails]."
msgstr "要安装最精简的用户空间，请使用 `FreeBSD-set-minimal-jail` 替代 `FreeBSD-set-base-jail`。以此方式安装的 jail 后续应使用 man:pkg[8] 而非 man:freebsd-update[8] 打补丁和升级；请参阅 crossref:jails[jail-upgrade-pkgbase, Upgrading pkgbase Jails]。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:687
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Base-system packages are a technology preview in FreeBSD 15.0.  The `FreeBSD-"
"base` repository is defined in [.filename]#/etc/pkg/FreeBSD.conf# but "
"disabled by default, so select it explicitly with `install -r FreeBSD-"
"base`.  The target root directory and its [.filename]#var/cache/pkg# and [."
"filename]#var/db/pkg# subdirectories may need to be created first.  The "
"traditional [.filename]#base.txz# distribution is still published for "
"FreeBSD 15.0, so the fetch-and-extract method continues to work there as "
"well."
msgstr "基础系统软件包在 FreeBSD 15.0 中属于技术预览。`FreeBSD-base` 仓库定义在 [.filename]#/etc/pkg/FreeBSD.conf# 中，但默认处于禁用状态，因此需使用 `install -r FreeBSD-base` 显式选择该仓库。可能需要先创建目标根目录及其 [.filename]#var/cache/pkg# 和 [.filename]#var/db/pkg# 子目录。FreeBSD 15.0 仍然发布传统的 [.filename]#base.txz# 发行版，因此获取并解压的方法在该版本中仍然可用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:691
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A userland built from a source tree can be installed into a jail's root "
"directory with the `DESTDIR` variable, which is the way to run a `-STABLE` "
"or custom-built userland in a jail.  After building the world, install it "
"and the remaining distribution files into the jail directory:"
msgstr "使用 `DESTDIR` 变量可以将从源代码树构建的用户空间安装到 jail 的根目录中，这是在 jail 中运行 `-STABLE` 或自定义构建用户空间的方法。完成 buildworld 后，将其余发行版文件一并安装到 jail 目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:698
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/src\n"
"# make buildworld\n"
"# make installworld DESTDIR=/usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"
"# make distribution DESTDIR=/usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/src\n# make buildworld\n# make installworld DESTDIR=/usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n# make distribution DESTDIR=/usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:703
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`make distribution` installs the default configuration files under the "
"jail's [.filename]#/etc# and is run only once, when populating the jail; "
"repeating it during an update would overwrite the configuration inside the "
"jail.  To update such a jail from source, follow the same sequence as for "
"the host: run `installworld` with the same `DESTDIR`, merge the "
"configuration files with `etcupdate -D` pointed at the jail's root "
"directory, and remove obsolete files and libraries with `make delete-old "
"delete-old-libs`, again with the same `DESTDIR`, rather than using man:"
"freebsd-update[8].  See crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld, Updating FreeBSD "
"from Source] for the complete source-update procedure."
msgstr "`make distribution` 会在 jail 的 [.filename]#/etc# 下安装默认配置文件，只应在填充 jail 时运行一次；在更新过程中重复运行会覆盖 jail 内的配置。要从源代码更新此类 jail，请按照与主机相同的步骤操作：使用相同的 `DESTDIR` 运行 `installworld`，使用指向 jail 根目录的 `etcupdate -D` 合并配置文件，然后再次使用相同的 `DESTDIR` 运行 `make delete-old delete-old-libs` 删除过时文件和库，而不要使用 man:freebsd-update[8]。完整的源代码更新流程请参阅 crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld, Updating FreeBSD from Source]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:705
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Cloning a Jail as a Template"
msgstr "将 jail 克隆为模板"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:708
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once a thick jail is fully configured, with packages installed, services "
"enabled, and local configuration in place, it can serve as a template image: "
"a template from which many identical jails are deployed almost instantly."
msgstr "厚型 jail 完成配置、安装软件包、启用服务并设置好本地配置后，可以用作模板映像：基于该模板几乎可以即时部署多个相同的 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:711
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On OpenZFS this is done by snapshotting the configured jail's dataset and "
"cloning it.  This requires the source jail to live on its own dataset, so "
"create it with `zfs create` rather than the `mkdir` used in the classic-jail "
"procedure above:"
msgstr "在 OpenZFS 上，可以通过对已配置 jail 的数据集创建快照并克隆来实现。源 jail 必须位于独立数据集中，因此应使用 `zfs create` 创建，而不是像上文经典 jail 的流程那样使用 `mkdir`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:715
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zfs create -p zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# zfs create -p zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:718
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Stop the jail before snapshotting so the image is consistent, then snapshot "
"and clone the dataset once for each new jail:"
msgstr "创建快照前先停止 jail，以确保映像状态一致，然后创建快照，并为每个新 jail 克隆一次数据集："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:724
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# service jail stop classic\n"
"# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/containers/classic@template\n"
"# zfs clone zroot/jails/containers/classic@template zroot/jails/containers/web1\n"
msgstr "# service jail stop classic\n# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/containers/classic@template\n# zfs clone zroot/jails/containers/classic@template zroot/jails/containers/web1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:727
#, fuzzy
msgid "On a UFS host, copy the configured jail's directory tree instead:"
msgstr "在使用 UFS 的主机上，则复制已配置 jail 的目录树："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:731
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cp -a /usr/local/jails/containers/classic /usr/local/jails/containers/web1\n"
msgstr "# cp -a /usr/local/jails/containers/classic /usr/local/jails/containers/web1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:735
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Each clone needs its own entry in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#, or in [."
"filename]#jail.conf.d#, with a unique name, path, and IP address.  Because "
"the `path` and `host.hostname` parameters in the example above are derived "
"from the block name with `${name}`, only the block name and the address "
"differ:"
msgstr "每个克隆都需要在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 或 [.filename]#jail.conf.d# 中拥有独立条目，并设置唯一的名称、路径和 IP 地址。由于上例中的 `path` 和 `host.hostname` 参数由块名称 `${name}` 派生，因此只需更改块名称和地址："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:743
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"web1 {\n"
"  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n"
"  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n"
"  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n"
"  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"
msgstr "web1 {\n  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:757
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # NETWORK\n"
"  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.152;\n"
"  interface = em0;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "  # NETWORK\n  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.152;\n  interface = em0;\n}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:763
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A template-image clone differs from a thin jail (crossref:jails[thin-jail, "
"Thin Jails]).  A thin jail keeps sharing a read-only base and is maintained "
"once at the template, whereas each template-image clone is a full, "
"independently writable copy that is patched and upgraded on its own as "
"described in crossref:jails[jail-upgrading, Jail Upgrading].  An OpenZFS "
"clone starts as a space-efficient copy-on-write copy that shares blocks with "
"the snapshot, and it keeps a dependency on that origin snapshot until `zfs "
"promote` severs it.  For a fully independent copy, or to replicate a jail to "
"another pool or host, use `zfs send` piped to `zfs receive` instead of `zfs "
"clone`."
msgstr "模板映像克隆不同于薄型 jail（crossref:jails[thin-jail, Thin Jails]）。薄型 jail 会继续共享只读基础系统，并在模板处统一维护；而每个模板映像克隆都是完整且可独立写入的副本，需要按照 crossref:jails[jail-upgrading, Jail Upgrading] 所述单独打补丁和升级。OpenZFS 克隆最初是节省空间的写时复制副本，与快照共享数据块；在使用 `zfs promote` 切断依赖之前，它仍依赖于源快照。若要获得完全独立的副本，或将 jail 复制到另一存储池或主机，请使用 `zfs send` 并将其传递给 `zfs receive`，而不是使用 `zfs clone`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:771
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Although Thin Jails use the same technology as Thick Jails, the creation "
"procedure is different.  Thin jails can be created using OpenZFS snapshots "
"or using templates and NullFS.  The use of OpenZFS snapshots and templates "
"using NullFS have certain advantages over classic jails, such as being able "
"to create them faster from snapshots or being able to update multiple jails "
"using NullFS."
msgstr "虽然薄型 jail 使用与厚型 jail 相同的技术，但创建流程不同。薄型 jail 可以使用 OpenZFS 快照创建，也可以使用模板和 NullFS 创建。与经典 jail 相比，OpenZFS 快照和 NullFS 模板各有优势，例如可以通过快照更快地创建 jail，或使用 NullFS 更新多个 jail。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:773
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Creating a Thin Jail Using OpenZFS Snapshots"
msgstr "使用 OpenZFS 快照创建薄型 jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:776
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Due to the good integration between FreeBSD and OpenZFS it is very easy to "
"create new Thin Jails using OpenZFS Snapshots."
msgstr "由于 FreeBSD 与 OpenZFS 集成良好，使用 OpenZFS 快照创建新的薄型 jail 非常容易。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:778
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To create a Thin Jail using OpenZFS Snapshots the first step is to create "
"the jail directory tree by following the instructions in crossref:jails[host-"
"configuration-directories, \"Setting Up the Jail Directory Tree\"]."
msgstr "要使用 OpenZFS 快照创建薄型 jail，第一步是按照 crossref:jails[host-configuration-directories, \"Setting Up the Jail Directory Tree\"] 中的说明创建 jail 目录树。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:782
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next, create a template.  Templates will only be used to create new jails.  "
"For this reason they are created in \"read-only\" mode so that jails are "
"created with an immutable base."
msgstr "接下来创建模板。模板仅用于创建新的 jail。因此，应以“只读”模式创建模板，使 jail 拥有不可变的基础系统。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:784
#, fuzzy
msgid "To create the dataset for the template, execute the following command:"
msgstr "执行以下命令创建模板数据集："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:788
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zfs create -p zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE\n"
msgstr "# zfs create -p zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:791
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:895
#, fuzzy
msgid "Then execute the following command to download the userland:"
msgstr "然后执行以下命令下载用户空间："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:798
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:902
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once the download is complete, it will be necessary to extract the contents "
"in the template directory by executing the following command:"
msgstr "下载完成后，需要执行以下命令将内容解压到模板目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:802
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# tar -xf /usr/local/jails/media/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base.txz -C /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE --unlink\n"
msgstr "# tar -xf /usr/local/jails/media/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base.txz -C /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE --unlink\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:805
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the userland extracted in the templates directory, it will be necessary "
"to copy the timezone and DNS server files to the template directory by "
"executing the following command:"
msgstr "将用户空间解压到模板目录后，需要执行以下命令，将时区和 DNS 服务器文件复制到模板目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:810
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cp /etc/resolv.conf /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/etc/resolv.conf\n"
"# cp /etc/localtime /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/etc/localtime\n"
msgstr "# cp /etc/resolv.conf /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/etc/resolv.conf\n# cp /etc/localtime /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/etc/localtime\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:813
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The next thing to do is update to the latest patch level by executing the "
"following command:"
msgstr "接下来，执行以下命令更新到最新的补丁级别："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:817
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1909
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/ fetch install\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/ fetch install\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:820
#, fuzzy
msgid "Once the update is finished, the template is ready."
msgstr "更新完成后，模板便准备就绪。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:822
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To create an OpenZFS Snapshot from the template, execute the following "
"command:"
msgstr "要从模板创建 OpenZFS 快照，请执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:826
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base\n"
msgstr "# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:829
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once the OpenZFS Snapshot has been created, infinite jails can be created "
"using the OpenZFS clone function."
msgstr "创建 OpenZFS 快照后，即可使用 OpenZFS 克隆功能创建任意数量的 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:831
#, fuzzy
msgid "To create a Thin Jail named `thinjail`, execute the following command:"
msgstr "要创建名为 `thinjail` 的精简 Jail，请执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:835
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zfs clone zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base zroot/jails/containers/thinjail\n"
msgstr "# zfs clone zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base zroot/jails/containers/thinjail\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:849
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1003
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"thinjail {\n"
"  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n"
"  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n"
"  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n"
"  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"
msgstr "thinjail {\n  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:863
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # NETWORK\n"
"  ip4 = inherit;\n"
"  interface = em0;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "  # NETWORK\n  ip4 = inherit;\n  interface = em0;\n}\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:870
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1040
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service jail start thinjail\n"
msgstr "# service jail start thinjail\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:876
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
