#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1034
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The [.filename]#fstab# file controls how man:mount_nullfs[8] presents the "
"base template and the skeleton inside the jail.  The base template is "
"mounted read-only (`ro`) so that every NullFS jail shares one immutable copy "
"of the base system.  The per-jail skeleton is mounted read-write (`rw`), "
"which is where each jail keeps its own writable [.filename]#/etc#, [."
"filename]#/var#, [.filename]#/usr/local#, and other local directories.  "
"Because all jails share that single read-only base template, updating the "
"one template updates every NullFS jail at once, in contrast to independent "
"OpenZFS clones which must each be updated separately."
msgstr "[.filename]#fstab# 文件控制 man:mount_nullfs[8] 如何在 jail 中呈现基础模板和 skeleton。基础模板以只读方式（`ro`）挂载，因此所有 NullFS jail 都共享同一份不可变的基础系统副本。每个 jail 的 skeleton 以读写方式（`rw`）挂载；每个 jail 自己可写的 [.filename]#/etc#、[.filename]#/var#、[.filename]#/usr/local# 及其他本地目录都存放于此。由于所有 jail 共享这份只读基础模板，更新该模板即可同时更新所有 NullFS jail；而独立的 OpenZFS 克隆则必须分别更新。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1046
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD VNET Jails have their own distinct networking stack, including "
"interfaces, IP addresses, routing tables, and firewall rules."
msgstr "FreeBSD VNET Jail 拥有各自独立的网络栈，包括接口、IP 地址、路由表和防火墙规则。"

#. type: Plain text
