"  exec.stop      = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n"
"  exec.poststop = \"/sbin/ifconfig ${bridge} deletem ${epair}a\";\n"
"  exec.poststop += \"/sbin/ifconfig ${epair}a destroy\";\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "  # ADD TO bridge INTERFACE\n  exec.prestart  = \"/sbin/ifconfig ${epair} create up\";\n  exec.prestart += \"/sbin/ifconfig ${epair}a up descr jail:${name}\";\n  exec.prestart += \"/sbin/ifconfig ${bridge} addm ${epair}a up\";\n  exec.start    += \"/sbin/ifconfig ${epair}b ${ip} up\";\n  exec.start    += \"/sbin/route add default ${gateway}\";\n  exec.start    += \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n  exec.stop      = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n  exec.poststop = \"/sbin/ifconfig ${bridge} deletem ${epair}a\";\n  exec.poststop += \"/sbin/ifconfig ${epair}a destroy\";\n}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1140
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A per-jail *unique* number used to derive both the epair device name (`epair"
"${id}`) and the last octet of the jail's address (`192.168.1.${id}`); give "
"each jail on the bridge a different value."
msgstr "每个 jail 使用一个独有的数字，用于生成 epair 设备名称（`epair${id}`）以及 jail 地址的最后一个八位组（`192.168.1.${id}`）；同一桥接上的每个 jail 都应使用不同的值。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1141
#, fuzzy
msgid "Refers to the bridge created previously."
msgstr "指向此前创建的桥接。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1145
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `vnet.interface` parameter names the interface that man:jail[8] moves "
"into the jail's network stack once the jail is created, here the jail side "
"of the epair, `${epair}b`.  That interface disappears from the host while "
"the jail runs and is automatically released back to the host when the jail "
"stops.  A physical network card or an SR-IOV virtual function can be handed "
"to a jail the same way, giving it dedicated networking without a bridge or "
"an epair."
msgstr "创建 jail 后，man:jail[8] 会将 `vnet.interface` 参数指定的接口移入 jail 的网络栈；此处指定的是 epair 的 jail 端 `${epair}b`。jail 运行期间，该接口会从主机上消失；jail 停止时，接口会自动释放并返回主机。也可以用同样的方式将物理网卡或 SR-IOV 虚拟功能分配给 jail，从而为其提供专用网络，而无需桥接或 epair。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1149
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `devfs_ruleset = 5` line applies the `devfsrules_jail_vnet` ruleset from "
"[.filename]#/etc/defaults/devfs.rules#, which extends the default jail "
"ruleset by exposing [.filename]#/dev/pf#.  A VNET jail can therefore run its "
"own man:pf[4] firewall with `pf_enable=\"YES\"` and a private [.filename]#pf."
"conf#, independent of the host.  See crossref:jails[jail-conf-devfs, Devfs "
"Rulesets] for how rulesets are defined and crossref:firewalls[firewalls, "
"Firewalls] for pf itself."
msgstr "`devfs_ruleset = 5` 这一行应用了 [.filename]#/etc/defaults/devfs.rules# 中的 `devfsrules_jail_vnet` 规则集；该规则集扩展了默认 jail 规则集，并公开 [.filename]#/dev/pf#。因此，VNET jail 可以通过 `pf_enable=\"YES\"` 和专用的 [.filename]#pf.conf# 运行自己的 man:pf[4] 防火墙，且不受主机影响。有关规则集的定义，请参阅 crossref:jails[jail-conf-devfs, Devfs Rulesets]；有关 pf 本身，请参阅 crossref:firewalls[firewalls, Firewalls]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1151
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Automating VNET Networking with jib"
msgstr "使用 jib 自动配置 VNET 网络"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1155
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Wiring up an epair and attaching it to the bridge by hand in `exec.prestart` "
"and `exec.poststop`, as shown above, becomes tedious across many jails.  The "
"base system ships a helper script, [.filename]#/usr/share/examples/jails/"
"jib#, that performs the same plumbing automatically."
msgstr "如上所示，在 `exec.prestart` 和 `exec.poststop` 中手动配置 epair 并将其连接到桥接，对于大量 jail 来说会变得繁琐。基本系统附带辅助脚本 [.filename]#/usr/share/examples/jails/jib#，可自动执行相同的配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1157
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Reference it from the jail's hooks instead of the five hand-rolled man:"
"ifconfig[8] lines:"
msgstr "在 jail 的钩子中引用该脚本，替代手动编写的五条 man:ifconfig[8] 命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1162
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  exec.prestart += \"jib addm ${name} em0\";\n"
"  exec.poststop += \"jib destroy ${name}\";\n"
msgstr "  exec.prestart += \"jib addm ${name} em0\";\n  exec.poststop += \"jib destroy ${name}\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1164
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  vnet.interface = \"e0b_${name}\";\n"
msgstr "  vnet.interface = \"e0b_${name}\";\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1170
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`jib addm` creates an epair whose host side is named `e0a_<name>` and whose "
"jail side is `e0b_<name>`, then attaches the host side to a bridge that it "
"creates automatically, named after the member interface (for `em0` the "
"bridge is `em0bridge`).  Name that jail side in `vnet.interface`.  When the "
"jail stops, `jib destroy` removes the epair.  The script also provides a "
"`jib show` subcommand to list the interfaces it manages."
msgstr "`jib addm` 会创建一个 epair，其主机端命名为 `e0a_<name>`，jail 端命名为 `e0b_<name>`，然后将主机端连接到一个自动创建的桥接；该桥接以成员接口命名（对于 `em0`，桥接名称为 `em0bridge`）。在 `vnet.interface` 中指定 jail 端的名称。jail 停止时，`jib destroy` 会移除 epair。该脚本还提供 `jib show` 子命令，用于列出它管理的接口。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1172
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Netgraph VNET Networking with jng"
msgstr "使用 jng 配置 Netgraph VNET 网络"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1176
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The third networking mode mentioned in the crossref:jails[jails-networking, "
"Networking] overview uses man:netgraph[4] instead of man:bridge[4] and "
"epair.  The base system ships a second helper, [.filename]#/usr/share/"
"examples/jails/jng#, that builds an `ng_bridge` connected to an `ng_eiface` "
"for each jail:"
msgstr "crossref:jails[jails-networking, Networking] 概述中提到的第三种网络模式使用 man:netgraph[4]，而不是 man:bridge[4] 和 epair。基本系统还附带另一个辅助脚本 [.filename]#/usr/share/examples/jails/jng#，可为每个 jail 创建一个连接到 `ng_eiface` 的 `ng_bridge`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1181
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  exec.prestart += \"jng bridge ${name} em0\";\n"
"  exec.poststop += \"jng shutdown ${name}\";\n"
msgstr "  exec.prestart += \"jng bridge ${name} em0\";\n  exec.poststop += \"jng shutdown ${name}\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1183
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  vnet.interface = \"ng0_${name}\";\n"
msgstr "  vnet.interface = \"ng0_${name}\";\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1187
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`jng bridge` creates the netgraph nodes and a jail-side interface named "
"`ng0_<name>`, which is named in `vnet.interface`; `jng shutdown` tears the "
"topology down when the jail stops.  The result is functionally equivalent to "
"the epair-and-bridge setup, but built on netgraph nodes rather than man:"
"bridge[4]."
msgstr "`jng bridge` 会创建 netgraph 节点和一个名为 `ng0_<name>` 的 jail 侧接口，该接口在 `vnet.interface` 中指定；jail 停止时，`jng shutdown` 会拆除网络拓扑。其功能等同于 epair 和网桥配置，但它基于 netgraph 节点，而不是 man:bridge[4]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1189
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Running a Firewall and DHCP inside a VNET Jail"
msgstr "在 VNET Jail 中运行防火墙和 DHCP"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1193
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Because `devfs_ruleset = 5` exposes [.filename]#/dev/pf#, a VNET jail can "
"run its own firewall.  Enable it inside the jail exactly as on any host, "
"with `pf_enable=\"YES\"` in the jail's [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# and its own "
"[.filename]#/etc/pf.conf#."
msgstr "由于 `devfs_ruleset = 5` 会公开 [.filename]#/dev/pf#，VNET jail 可以运行自己的防火墙。只需像在任何主机上一样，在 jail 的 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中设置 `pf_enable=\"YES\"`，并配置自己的 [.filename]#/etc/pf.conf#，即可在 jail 中启用防火墙。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1197
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ruleset 5 does not expose [.filename]#/dev/bpf#, however.  A VNET jail that "
"obtains its address over DHCP, for example with `ifconfig_e0b_myjail="
"\"SYNCDHCP\"` in its [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#, runs man:dhclient[8], which "
"needs bpf and therefore fails under ruleset 5.  Following the recipe in "
"crossref:jails[jail-conf-devfs,Devfs Rulesets], define a custom ruleset in [."
"filename]#/etc/devfs.rules# that starts from `devfsrules_jail_vnet` and "
"additionally unhides the bpf devices:"
msgstr "不过，规则集 5 不会公开 [.filename]#/dev/bpf#。通过 DHCP 获取地址的 VNET jail（例如在其 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中设置 `ifconfig_e0b_myjail=\"SYNCDHCP\"`）会运行 man:dhclient[8]；该程序需要 bpf，因此在规则集 5 下会失败。请按照 crossref:jails[jail-conf-devfs,Devfs Rulesets] 中的步骤，在 [.filename]#/etc/devfs.rules# 中定义一个自定义规则集：以 `devfsrules_jail_vnet` 为基础，并额外取消隐藏 bpf 设备："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1203
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[devfsrules_jail_vnet_dhcp=101]\n"
"add include $devfsrules_jail_vnet\n"
"add path 'bpf*' unhide\n"
msgstr "[devfsrules_jail_vnet_dhcp=101]\nadd include $devfsrules_jail_vnet\nadd path 'bpf*' unhide\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1206
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After running `service devfs restart` on the host, point the jail at the new "
"ruleset with `devfs_ruleset = 101;`."
msgstr "在主机上运行 `service devfs restart` 后，使用 `devfs_ruleset = 101;` 将 jail 配置为使用新的规则集。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1214
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD can run a Linux userland inside a jail using crossref:"
"linuxemu[linuxemu,Linux Binary Compatibility] and package:sysutils/"
"debootstrap[].  Jails do not have a kernel.  They run on the host's kernel.  "
"Therefore it is necessary to enable Linux Binary Compatibility in the host "
"system."
msgstr "FreeBSD 可以通过 crossref:linuxemu[linuxemu,Linux Binary Compatibility] 和 package:sysutils/debootstrap[] 在 jail 中运行 Linux 用户空间。Jail 没有内核，而是运行在主机的内核上。因此，必须在主机系统中启用 Linux 二进制兼容功能。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1216
#, fuzzy
msgid "To enable the Linux ABI at boot time, execute the following command:"
msgstr "要在启动时启用 Linux ABI，请执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1220
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "# sysrc linux_enable=\"YES\"\n"
msgstr "named_enable=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1223
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once enabled, it can be started without rebooting by executing the following "
"command:"
msgstr "启用后，可以执行以下命令，无需重新启动即可启动该功能："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1227
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service linux start\n"
msgstr "# service linux start\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1231
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The next step is to create a jail as indicated above, for example as in "
"crossref:jails[creating-thin-jail-openzfs-snapshots, Creating a Thin Jail "
"Using OpenZFS Snapshots], but *without* performing the configuration.  "
"FreeBSD Linux jails require a specific configuration that is detailed below."
msgstr "下一步是按照上述说明创建一个 jail，例如参照 crossref:jails[creating-thin-jail-openzfs-snapshots, Creating a Thin Jail Using OpenZFS Snapshots]，但*不要*进行配置。FreeBSD Linux jail 需要特定配置，详情如下。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1233
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the host does not already have an [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# — for "
"example on a system whose jails so far have been created only from the "
"command line — create an empty one so that man:service[8] can stop the jail "
"later:"
msgstr "如果主机上还没有 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#（例如，系统上的 jail 之前都只通过命令行创建），请创建一个空文件，以便 man:service[8] 稍后能够停止 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1237
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# touch /etc/jail.conf\n"
msgstr "# touch /etc/jail.conf\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1241
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man:service[8] jail script reads [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# when "
"stopping a jail, so the stop command fails if the file does not exist.  If "
"an [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# is already present from an earlier section, "
"this step is not needed."
msgstr "停止 jail 时，man:service[8] 的 jail 脚本会读取 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#，因此如果该文件不存在，停止命令就会失败。如果前面的章节已经创建了 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#，则无需执行此步骤。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1244
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following man:jail[8] command performs the required configuration for "
"the jail and starts it directly, without a [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# "
"entry.  The `-c` flag creates a new jail and `-m` modifies an existing one; "
"combined as `-cm`, man:jail[8] creates the jail if it does not yet exist and "
"updates it if it does:"
msgstr "以下 man:jail[8] 命令会为 jail 执行所需配置并直接启动它，而无需在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中添加条目。`-c` 标志用于创建新 jail，`-m` 用于修改现有 jail；组合为 `-cm` 后，man:jail[8] 会在 jail 尚不存在时创建它，在 jail 已存在时更新它："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1265
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# jail -cm \\\n"
"    name=ubuntu \\\n"
"    host.hostname=\"ubuntu.example.com\" \\\n"
"    path=\"/usr/local/jails/containers/ubuntu\" \\\n"
"    interface=\"em0\" \\\n"
"    ip4.addr=\"192.168.1.155\" \\\n"
"    exec.start=\"/bin/sh /etc/rc\" \\\n"
"    exec.stop=\"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\" \\\n"
"    mount.devfs \\\n"
"    devfs_ruleset=4 \\\n"
"    allow.mount \\\n"
"    allow.mount.devfs \\\n"
"    allow.mount.fdescfs \\\n"
"    allow.mount.procfs \\\n"
"    allow.mount.linprocfs \\\n"
"    allow.mount.linsysfs \\\n"
"    allow.mount.tmpfs \\\n"
"    enforce_statfs=1\n"
msgstr "# jail -cm \\\n    name=ubuntu \\\n    host.hostname=\"ubuntu.example.com\" \\\n    path=\"/usr/local/jails/containers/ubuntu\" \\\n    interface=\"em0\" \\\n    ip4.addr=\"192.168.1.155\" \\\n    exec.start=\"/bin/sh /etc/rc\" \\\n    exec.stop=\"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\" \\\n    mount.devfs \\\n    devfs_ruleset=4 \\\n    allow.mount \\\n    allow.mount.devfs \\\n    allow.mount.fdescfs \\\n    allow.mount.procfs \\\n    allow.mount.linprocfs \\\n    allow.mount.linsysfs \\\n    allow.mount.tmpfs \\\n    enforce_statfs=1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1268
#, fuzzy
msgid "Access the newly created jail as `root` with man:jexec[8]:"
msgstr "使用 man:jexec[8] 以 `root` 身份访问刚创建的 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1272
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jexec -u root ubuntu sh\n"
msgstr "# jexec -u root ubuntu sh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1277
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Inside the jail, install package:sysutils/debootstrap[] and use it to build "
"the Ubuntu userland under [.filename]#/compat/ubuntu#.  package:sysutils/"
"debootstrap[] is the tool that builds the Linux userland; it is not required "
"to enter the jail afterward.  Running man:pkg[7] for the first time "
"bootstraps it automatically:"
msgstr "在 jail 中安装 package:sysutils/debootstrap[]，并使用它在 [.filename]#/compat/ubuntu# 下构建 Ubuntu 用户空间。package:sysutils/debootstrap[] 是用于构建 Linux 用户空间的工具；之后进入 jail 时不需要它。首次运行 man:pkg[7] 时会自动进行引导安装："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1282
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# pkg install debootstrap\n"
"# debootstrap jammy /compat/ubuntu\n"
msgstr "# pkg install debootstrap\n# debootstrap jammy /compat/ubuntu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1286
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`jammy` selects Ubuntu 22.04 LTS.  A newer LTS such as `noble` (Ubuntu "
"24.04) can be selected instead, provided it runs under the linuxulator."
msgstr "`jammy` 表示 Ubuntu 22.04 LTS。也可以改用较新的 LTS 版本，例如 `noble`（Ubuntu 24.04），前提是它能在 linuxulator 下运行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1289
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When the process has finished and the message `Base system installed "
"successfully` is displayed on the console, stop the jail from the host "
"system.  Because this jail is not enabled in [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# and "
"not yet listed in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#, use the `one`-prefixed man:"
"service[8] action, which runs even for a jail that is not enabled:"
msgstr "进程结束并且控制台显示 `Base system installed successfully` 消息后，从主机系统停止 jail。由于此 jail 尚未在 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中启用，也尚未列入 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf#，请使用前缀为 `one` 的 man:service[8] 操作；即使 jail 未启用，该操作也会运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1293
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service jail onestop ubuntu\n"
msgstr "# service jail onestop ubuntu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1296
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `onestart` and `onestop` actions are the counterparts of `start` and "
"`stop` for jails that are not enabled through `jail_enable` or listed in "
"`jail_list`."
msgstr "对于未通过 `jail_enable` 启用或未列入 `jail_list` 的 jail，`onestart` 和 `onestop` 操作分别对应 `start` 和 `stop`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1298
#, fuzzy
msgid "Then add an entry in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# for the Linux jail:"
msgstr "然后在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中为 Linux jail 添加条目："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1306
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ubuntu {\n"
"  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n"
"  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n"
"  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n"
"  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"
msgstr "ubuntu {\n  # STARTUP/LOGGING\n  exec.start = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc\";\n  exec.stop = \"/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown\";\n  exec.consolelog = \"/var/log/jail_console_${name}.log\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1312
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # PERMISSIONS\n"
"  allow.raw_sockets;\n"
"  exec.clean;\n"
"  mount.devfs;\n"
"  devfs_ruleset = 4;\n"
msgstr "  # PERMISSIONS\n  allow.raw_sockets;\n  exec.clean;\n  mount.devfs;\n  devfs_ruleset = 4;\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1320
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # NETWORK\n"
"  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.155;\n"
"  interface = em0;\n"
msgstr "  # NETWORK\n  ip4.addr = 192.168.1.155;\n  interface = em0;\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1330
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  # MOUNT\n"
"  mount += \"devfs     $path/compat/ubuntu/dev     devfs     rw  0 0\";\n"
"  mount += \"tmpfs     $path/compat/ubuntu/dev/shm tmpfs     rw,size=1g,mode=1777  0 0\";\n"
"  mount += \"fdescfs   $path/compat/ubuntu/dev/fd  fdescfs   rw,linrdlnk 0 0\";\n"
"  mount += \"linprocfs $path/compat/ubuntu/proc    linprocfs rw  0 0\";\n"
"  mount += \"linsysfs  $path/compat/ubuntu/sys     linsysfs  rw  0 0\";\n"
"  mount += \"/tmp      $path/compat/ubuntu/tmp     nullfs    rw  0 0\";\n"
"  mount += \"/home     $path/compat/ubuntu/home    nullfs    rw  0 0\";\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "  # MOUNT\n  mount += \"devfs     $path/compat/ubuntu/dev     devfs     rw  0 0\";\n  mount += \"tmpfs     $path/compat/ubuntu/dev/shm tmpfs     rw,size=1g,mode=1777  0 0\";\n  mount += \"fdescfs   $path/compat/ubuntu/dev/fd  fdescfs   rw,linrdlnk 0 0\";\n  mount += \"linprocfs $path/compat/ubuntu/proc    linprocfs rw  0 0\";\n  mount += \"linsysfs  $path/compat/ubuntu/sys     linsysfs  rw  0 0\";\n  mount += \"/tmp      $path/compat/ubuntu/tmp     nullfs    rw  0 0\";\n  mount += \"/home     $path/compat/ubuntu/home    nullfs    rw  0 0\";\n}\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1337
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The jail can also present a specific Linux kernel identity to the programs "
"running inside it.  The `linux` parameter selects whether the jail inherits "
"the host's Linux emulation environment (`inherit`) or gets its own (`new`), "
"and `linux.osname`, `linux.osrelease`, and `linux.oss_version` set the OS "
"name, release, and OSS version that Linux binaries see.  For example, `linux."
"osrelease=6.1.0` makes man:uname[1] and version-checking Linux programs "
"inside the jail report that kernel release instead of the host-wide `compat."
"linux.osrelease` value."
msgstr "Jail 还可以向其中运行的程序呈现特定的 Linux 内核标识。`linux` 参数用于选择 jail 是继承主机的 Linux 仿真环境（`inherit`），还是使用自己的环境（`new`）；`linux.osname`、`linux.osrelease` 和 `linux.oss_version` 则设置 Linux 二进制程序所看到的操作系统名称、发行版本和 OSS 版本。例如，设置 `linux.osrelease=6.1.0` 后，jail 中的 man:uname[1] 和检查版本的 Linux 程序会报告该内核发行版本，而不是主机范围内的 `compat.linux.osrelease` 值。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1340
#, fuzzy
msgid "Then the jail can be started as usual with the following command:"
msgstr "然后可以像往常一样使用以下命令启动 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1344
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service jail start ubuntu\n"
msgstr "# service jail start ubuntu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1347
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ubuntu environment can be accessed using the following command:"
msgstr "可以使用以下命令访问 Ubuntu 环境："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1351
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jexec ubuntu chroot /compat/ubuntu /bin/bash\n"
msgstr "# jexec ubuntu chroot /compat/ubuntu /bin/bash\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1354
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"More information can be found in the chapter crossref:linuxemu[linuxemu,"
"Linux Binary Compatibility]."
msgstr "更多信息请参阅 crossref:linuxemu[linuxemu,Linux Binary Compatibility] 章节。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1356
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "NAT and Port Forwarding for Jails"
msgstr "Jail 的 NAT 和端口转发"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1360
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A jail that is given a private address — on a cloned man:lo[4] interface "
"such as `lo1`, on a private bridge, or on a VNET epair on an internal "
"network — has no route to the internet of its own.  The host must translate "
"the jail's traffic to a routable address, and, to reach a service running "
"inside such a jail from outside, redirect incoming connections to the jail."
msgstr "如果 jail 被分配了私有地址（例如位于克隆的 man:lo[4] 接口 `lo1`、私有网桥，或内部网络上的 VNET epair），它本身就没有通往互联网的路由。主机必须将 jail 的流量转换为可路由的地址；若要从外部访问此类 jail 中运行的服务，还必须将传入连接重定向到 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1363
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, allow the host to forward packets between its interfaces.  Enable it "
"at boot and immediately with the following commands:"
msgstr "首先，允许主机在其接口之间转发数据包。使用以下命令设置为在启动时启用并立即生效："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1368
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# sysrc gateway_enable=\"YES\"\n"
"# sysctl net.inet.ip.forwarding=1\n"
msgstr "# sysrc gateway_enable=\"YES\"\n# sysctl net.inet.ip.forwarding=1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1371
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For IPv6, use `ipv6_gateway_enable=\"YES\"` and `net.inet6.ip6.forwarding=1`."
msgstr "对于 IPv6，请使用 `ipv6_gateway_enable=\"YES\"` 和 `net.inet6.ip6.forwarding=1`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1374
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then configure Network Address Translation on the host with man:pf[4].  The "
"following [.filename]#/etc/pf.conf# gives every jail on the private "
"`192.168.0.0/24` network outbound access through the host's external "
"interface `em0`, and publishes a jailed web server on the host's port 80:"
msgstr "然后使用 man:pf[4] 在主机上配置网络地址转换。以下 [.filename]#/etc/pf.conf# 会让私有网络 `192.168.0.0/24` 上的所有 jail 通过主机外部接口 `em0` 访问外部网络，并将 jail 中的 Web 服务器发布到主机的 80 端口："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1378
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ext_if = \"em0\"\n"
msgstr "ext_if = \"em0\"\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1381
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# Translate outbound jail traffic to the host address\n"
"nat on $ext_if from 192.168.0.0/24 to any -> ($ext_if)\n"
msgstr "# Translate outbound jail traffic to the host address\nnat on $ext_if from 192.168.0.0/24 to any -> ($ext_if)\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1384
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# Forward inbound web traffic to the jailed server\n"
"rdr on $ext_if proto tcp to port 80 -> 192.168.0.151\n"
msgstr "# Forward inbound web traffic to the jailed server\nrdr on $ext_if proto tcp to port 80 -> 192.168.0.151\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1387
#, fuzzy
msgid "The `rdr` target must be the jail's own address."
msgstr "`rdr` 的目标必须是 jail 自身的地址。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1389
#, fuzzy
msgid "Enable and start man:pf[4] with the following commands:"
msgstr "使用以下命令启用并启动 man:pf[4]："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1394
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# sysrc pf_enable=\"YES\"\n"
"# service pf start\n"
msgstr "named_enable=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1400
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD 15.0 adds the OpenBSD-style inline `nat-to` and `rdr-to` syntax, "
"which attaches translation to a `pass` or `match` rule, for example `match "
"out on $ext_if from 192.168.0.0/24 to any nat-to ($ext_if)`.  The classic "
"`nat on` and `rdr on` rules shown above work on both FreeBSD 14.x and 15.x."
msgstr "FreeBSD 15.0 新增了 OpenBSD 风格的内联 `nat-to` 和 `rdr-to` 语法，可将转换附加到 `pass` 或 `match` 规则中，例如 `match out on $ext_if from 192.168.0.0/24 to any nat-to ($ext_if)`。上文所示的传统 `nat on` 和 `rdr on` 规则同时适用于 FreeBSD 14.x 和 15.x。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1403
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For the full treatment of man:pf[4] and man:ipfw[8], including complete rule "
"sets and man:ipfw[8]-based NAT, see crossref:firewalls[firewalls,Firewalls]."
msgstr "有关 man:pf[4] 和 man:ipfw[8] 的完整说明，包括完整规则集和基于 man:ipfw[8] 的 NAT，请参阅 crossref:firewalls[firewalls,Firewalls]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1413
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Service jails are available since FreeBSD 15.0.  A service jail is "
"configured completely via [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# or man:sysrc[8].  The "
"base system services are service jails ready.  They contain a config line "
"which enables networking or lifts other restrictions of jails.  Base system "
"services which do not make sense to run inside jails are configured to not "
"be started as a service jail, even if enabled in [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#.  "
"Some examples of such a service are services which want to mount or unmount "
"something in the start or stop method, or only configure something like a "
"route, or firewall, or the like."
msgstr "从 FreeBSD 15.0 起提供服务 jail。服务 jail 完全通过 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 或 man:sysrc[8] 进行配置。基本系统服务均已准备好在服务 jail 中运行。它们包含用于启用网络或解除 jail 其他限制的配置行。对于不适合在 jail 中运行的基本系统服务，即使已在 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中启用，也不会将其配置为以服务 jail 方式启动。这类服务包括在启动或停止方法中需要挂载或卸载内容、只负责配置路由或防火墙等项目的服务。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1416
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Third party services may or may not be service jails ready.  To check if a "
"service is service jail ready, the following command can be used:"
msgstr "第三方服务可能已准备好在服务 jail 中运行，也可能没有。可以使用以下命令检查某项服务是否已准备好在服务 jail 中运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1420
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# grep _svcj_options /path/to/rc.d/servicename\n"
msgstr "# grep _svcj_options /path/to/rc.d/servicename\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1423
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If there is no output, the service is not service jail ready, or does not "
"need any additional privileges like for example, network access."
msgstr "如果没有输出，则表示该服务尚未准备好在服务 jail 中运行，或者不需要网络访问等额外权限。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1425
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the service is not service jail ready, and needs network access, it can "
"be made ready by adding the necessary config to [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#:"
msgstr "如果某项服务尚未准备好在服务 jail 中运行，但需要网络访问，可以在 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中添加必要的配置，使其具备相应条件："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1429
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sysrc servicename_svcj_options=net_basic\n"
msgstr "# sysrc servicename_svcj_options=net_basic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1432
#, fuzzy
msgid "For all possible `_svcj_options` see the man:rc.conf[5] man-page."
msgstr "所有可用的 `_svcj_options` 请参阅 man:rc.conf[5] 手册页。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1435
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To enable a service jail for a given service, the service needs to be "
"stopped and the `servicename_svcj` variable needs to be set to YES.  To put "
"man:syslogd[8] into a service jail, use the following sequence of commands:"
msgstr "要为某项服务启用服务 jail，必须先停止该服务，然后将 `servicename_svcj` 变量设置为 YES。要将 man:syslogd[8] 放入服务 jail，请按以下顺序执行命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1441
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# service syslogd stop\n"
"# sysrc syslogd_svcj=YES\n"
"# service syslogd start\n"
msgstr "# service syslogd stop\n# sysrc syslogd_svcj=YES\n# service syslogd start\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1445
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the `servicename_svcj` variable is changed, the service needs to be "
"stopped before it is changed.  If it is not stopped, the rc framework will "
"not detect the correct state of the service and will not be able to do what "
"is requested."
msgstr "如果要更改 `servicename_svcj` 变量，必须先停止服务再进行更改。如果服务未停止，rc 框架将无法检测到服务的正确状态，也就无法执行请求的操作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1448
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Service jails are managed only via man:rc.conf[5]/man:sysrc[8] and the man:"
"service[8] command.  The jail utilities, like man:jls[8] as described in "
"crossref:jails[jail-management,Jail Management], can be used to investigate "
"the operation, but the man:jail[8] command is not supposed to be used to "
"manage them."
msgstr "服务 jail 只能通过 man:rc.conf[5]/man:sysrc[8] 和 man:service[8] 命令管理。可以使用 jail 工具（例如 man:jls[8]，详见 crossref:jails[jail-management,Jail Management]）检查其运行情况，但不应使用 man:jail[8] 命令管理服务 jail。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1450
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Jail Management"
msgstr "Jail 管理"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1454
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once the jail is created, there are a number of operations that can be "
"performed, like starting, rebooting or deleting the jail, installing "
"software in it, etc.  In this section the different actions that can be done "
"with jails from the host will be described."
msgstr "创建 jail 后，可以执行多种操作，例如启动、重新启动或删除 jail，以及在其中安装软件等。本节将介绍如何从主机对 jail 执行各种操作。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1456
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Creating Jails"
msgid "List Running Jails"
msgstr "建立 Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1459
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To list the jails that are running on the host system, the command man:"
"jls[8] can be used:"
msgstr "要列出主机系统上正在运行的 jail，可以使用 man:jls[8] 命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1463
