#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1523
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "How to build, start, and stop a jail."
msgid "Start, Restart, and Stop a Jail"
msgstr "如何联编、 启动和停止 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1526
#, fuzzy
msgid "man:service[8] is used to start, reboot, or stop a jail on the host."
msgstr "使用 man:service[8] 在主机上启动、重启或停止 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1528
#, fuzzy
msgid "For example, to start a jail, run the following command:"
msgstr "例如，要启动一个 jail，请运行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1532
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service jail start jailname\n"
msgstr "# service jail start jailname\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1535
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Change the `start` argument to `restart` or `stop` to perform other actions "
"on the jail."
msgstr "将 `start` 参数改为 `restart` 或 `stop`，即可对 jail 执行其他操作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1542
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Stopping a jail is more than killing the processes inside it.  When a jail "
"is stopped, man:jail[8] first runs the commands in its `exec.stop` parameter "
"— typically `/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown` — inside the jail so that its "
"services shut down cleanly.  It then sends `SIGTERM` to any processes still "
"running in the jail and waits up to `stop.timeout` seconds (10 by default) "
"for them to exit.  Once that time has passed, the jail is removed, which "
"kills whatever remains with `SIGKILL`.  If `stop.timeout` is set to zero, no "
"`SIGTERM` is sent and the jail is removed immediately.  This is why a jail "
"with a slow-stopping daemon can appear to hang for ten seconds while it "
"stops; raise `stop.timeout` in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# for a jail that "
"runs a database or another service that needs longer to shut down gracefully."
msgstr "停止 jail 不只是结束其中的进程。停止 jail 时，man:jail[8] 首先会在 jail 内运行其 `exec.stop` 参数中的命令（通常为 `/bin/sh /etc/rc.shutdown`），以便其服务正常关闭。然后，它会向 jail 中仍在运行的进程发送 `SIGTERM`，并等待最多 `stop.timeout` 秒（默认为 10 秒），让这些进程退出。等待时间结束后，jail 将被移除，剩余进程会被 `SIGKILL` 结束。如果将 `stop.timeout` 设为零，则不会发送 `SIGTERM`，而是立即移除 jail。因此，运行着停止较慢的守护进程的 jail 在停止时可能会看起来卡住十秒；对于运行数据库或其他需要较长时间才能正常关闭的服务的 jail，请在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中调高 `stop.timeout`。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1544
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Destroy a Jail"
msgstr "销毁 jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1547
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Destroying a jail is not as simple as stopping the jail using man:service[8] "
"and removing the jail directory and [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# entry."
msgstr "销毁 jail 并不像使用 man:service[8] 停止 jail，再删除 jail 目录和 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中的条目那么简单。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1552
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD takes system security very seriously.  For this reason there are "
"certain files that not even the root user can delete.  This functionality is "
"known as File Flags.  On a jail whose files live on a UFS file system, these "
"flags must be cleared before the jail directory can be removed."
msgstr "FreeBSD 非常重视系统安全。因此，有些文件连 root 用户也无法删除。这项功能称为文件标志。对于文件存放在 UFS 文件系统上的 jail，必须先清除这些标志，才能删除 jail 目录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1554
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first step is to stop the desired jail executing the following command:"
msgstr "第一步是停止目标 jail，运行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1558
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service jail stop classic\n"
msgstr "# service jail stop classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1561
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The second step is to remove these flags with man:chflags[1] by executing "
"the following command, in which `classic` is the name of the jail to remove:"
msgstr "第二步是使用 man:chflags[1] 清除这些标志。运行以下命令，其中 `classic` 是要删除的 jail 的名称："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1565
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# chflags -R 0 /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# chflags -R 0 /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1568
#, fuzzy
msgid "The third step is to delete the directory where the jail was:"
msgstr "第三步是删除 jail 所在的目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1572
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# rm -rf /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# rm -rf /usr/local/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1577
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The two steps above apply to a jail stored on a UFS file system.  A jail "
"backed by its own ZFS dataset — as created in crossref:jails[host-"
"configuration-directories,Setting Up the Jail Directory Tree] — is removed "
"by destroying the dataset instead.  Dataset destruction is not blocked by "
"file flags, so the man:chflags[1] step is unnecessary in this case:"
msgstr "上述两步适用于存储在 UFS 文件系统上的 jail。由其自身 ZFS 数据集支持的 jail（如 crossref:jails[host-configuration-directories,Setting Up the Jail Directory Tree] 中创建的 jail），则通过销毁该数据集来移除。销毁数据集不受文件标志限制，因此此时不需要执行 man:chflags[1] 这一步："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1582
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# service jail stop classic\n"
"# zfs destroy zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# service jail stop classic\n# zfs destroy zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1585
#, fuzzy
msgid "Add `-r` to also destroy any snapshots the dataset holds."
msgstr "添加 `-r` 还会销毁该数据集包含的所有快照。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1591
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A ZFS thin jail created by cloning a template snapshot (see crossref:"
"jails[thin-jail,Thin Jails]) depends on that snapshot.  While any clone "
"still exists, man:zfs[8] refuses to destroy the template snapshot and prints "
"the list of dependent clones.  To retire a template, first destroy every "
"jail cloned from it, or run `zfs promote` on a clone so it no longer depends "
"on the template."
msgstr "通过克隆模板快照创建的 ZFS thin jail（参见 crossref:jails[thin-jail,Thin Jails]）依赖于该快照。只要仍有克隆存在，man:zfs[8] 就会拒绝销毁模板快照，并列出依赖它的克隆。要停用模板，请先销毁从该模板克隆的所有 jail，或在某个克隆上运行 `zfs promote`，使其不再依赖该模板。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1595
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Finally, in either case, remove the jail entry in [.filename]#/etc/jail."
"conf# or in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d#.  For a NullFS thin jail, also "
"delete its [.filename]#.fstab# file and its now-empty mountpoint directory."
msgstr "最后，无论是哪种情况，都要从 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 或 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d# 中删除 jail 条目。对于 NullFS thin jail，还要删除其 [.filename]#.fstab# 文件和现已空置的挂载点目录。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1597
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Handle Packages in a Jail"
msgstr "管理 jail 中的软件包"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1600
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man:pkg[8] tool supports the `-j` argument in order to handle packages "
"installed inside the jail."
msgstr "man:pkg[8] 工具支持 `-j` 参数，用于管理安装在 jail 内的软件包。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1602
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For example, to install package:www/nginx-lite[] in the jail, the next "
"command can be executed *from the host*:"
msgstr "例如，要在 jail 中安装 package:www/nginx-lite[]，可以在*主机上*运行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1606
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# pkg -j classic install nginx-lite\n"
msgstr "# pkg -j classic install nginx-lite\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1609
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For more information on working with packages in FreeBSD, see crossref:"
"ports[ports,\"Installing Applications: Packages and Ports\"]."
msgstr "有关在 FreeBSD 中使用软件包的更多信息，请参见 crossref:ports[ports,\"Installing Applications: Packages and Ports\"]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1611
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Managing Services in a Jail from the Host"
msgstr "从主机管理 jail 中的服务"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1615
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Services inside a jail can be enabled and controlled from the host without "
"first entering the jail with man:jexec[8].  Both man:service[8] and man:"
"sysrc[8] accept a `-j` argument that names the target jail by ID or name and "
"operates on that jail's man:rc[8] configuration."
msgstr "无需先使用 man:jexec[8] 进入 jail，即可在主机上启用和控制 jail 内的服务。man:service[8] 和 man:sysrc[8] 都接受 `-j` 参数，用于按 ID 或名称指定目标 jail，并操作该 jail 的 man:rc[8] 配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1617
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Continuing the package example above, enable and start nginx in the "
"`classic` jail directly from the host:"
msgstr "继续使用上面的软件包示例，直接在主机上启用并启动 `classic` jail 中的 nginx："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1622
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# sysrc -j classic nginx_enable=YES\n"
"# service -j classic nginx start\n"
msgstr "# sysrc -j classic nginx_enable=YES\n# service -j classic nginx start\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1625
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"These commands have the same effect as running man:sysrc[8] and man:"
"service[8] through man:jexec[8], but they keep host-side administration and "
"scripting uniform with an unjailed system."
msgstr "这些命令的效果与通过 man:jexec[8] 运行 man:sysrc[8] 和 man:service[8] 相同，但能让主机端的管理和脚本操作与非 jail 系统保持一致。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1627
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Access a Jail"
msgstr "访问 jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1630
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While it has been stated above that it is best to manage jails from the host "
"system, a jail can be entered with man:jexec[8]."
msgstr "虽然上文提到最好从主机系统管理 jail，但也可以使用 man:jexec[8] 进入 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1632
#, fuzzy
msgid "The jail can be entered by running man:jexec[8] from the host:"
msgstr "可以在主机上运行 man:jexec[8] 进入 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1636
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jexec -u root jailname\n"
msgstr "# jexec -u root jailname\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1642
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `-u` flag selects the user to run as, resolving the name against the "
"*host* password database.  To resolve the user against the *jail's* own "
"password database instead, use `-U`.  When no command is given, as here, man:"
"jexec[8] starts that user's login shell inside the jail.  Add `-l` to run it "
"in a clean login environment that keeps only `HOME`, `SHELL`, `TERM`, and "
"`USER`, resets `PATH` to [.filename]#/bin:/usr/bin#, and behaves like a "
"fresh login; `-d` sets the working directory, which defaults to the jail "
"root."
msgstr "`-u` 标志用于选择要以其身份运行的用户，并根据*主机*的密码数据库解析用户名。若要改为根据*jail 自身*的密码数据库解析用户名，请使用 `-U`。如本例所示，如果没有指定命令，man:jexec[8] 会在 jail 内启动该用户的登录 shell。添加 `-l` 可在干净的登录环境中运行，仅保留 `HOME`、`SHELL`、`TERM` 和 `USER`，将 `PATH` 重置为 [.filename]#/bin:/usr/bin#，其行为与全新登录相同；`-d` 用于设置工作目录，默认为 jail 根目录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1644
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When gaining access to the jail, the message configured in man:motd[5] will "
"be displayed."
msgstr "进入 jail 时，会显示 man:motd[5] 中配置的消息。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1646
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Execute Commands in a Jail"
msgstr "在 jail 中执行命令"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1649
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To execute a command from the host system in a jail the man:jexec[8] can be "
"used."
msgstr "可以使用 man:jexec[8] 在 jail 中执行主机系统的命令。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1651
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For example, to stop a service that is running inside a jail, the command "
"will be executed:"
msgstr "例如，要停止在 jail 内运行的服务，请执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1655
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jexec -l jailname service nginx stop\n"
msgstr "# jexec -l jailname service nginx stop\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1658
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Viewing Jailed Processes and Sockets from the Host"
msgstr "从主机查看 jail 中的进程和套接字"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1661
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"From the host, the processes and sockets of every jail are visible and can "
"be filtered by jail."
msgstr "在主机上可以查看所有 jail 中的进程和套接字，并按 jail 进行筛选。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1663
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:ps[1] accepts `-J` to restrict its output to a single jail, given by JID "
"or name:"
msgstr "man:ps[1] 接受 `-J` 参数，可将输出限制为单个 jail，该 jail 可通过 JID 或名称指定："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1667
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# ps -J classic\n"
msgstr "# ps -J classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1670
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The output should be similar to the following, where the `J` in the `STAT` "
"column marks a process that is running in a jail:"
msgstr "输出应类似于以下内容，其中 `STAT` 列中的 `J` 表示该进程正在 jail 中运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1675
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
" PID TT  STAT    TIME COMMAND\n"
"2841  -  IsJ  0:00.02 /usr/sbin/syslogd -ss\n"
"2903  -  IsJ  0:00.00 nginx: master process /usr/local/sbin/nginx\n"
msgstr " PID TT  STAT    TIME COMMAND\n2841  -  IsJ  0:00.02 /usr/sbin/syslogd -ss\n2903  -  IsJ  0:00.00 nginx: master process /usr/local/sbin/nginx\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1680
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use `ps -J 0` to show only the host's own processes.  The `jail` and `jid` "
"keywords can also be added to the `-o` output format to show which jail each "
"process belongs to.  For example, to list every process on the host together "
"with its jail:"
msgstr "使用 `ps -J 0` 仅显示主机自身的进程。也可以将 `jail` 和 `jid` 关键字加入 `-o` 输出格式，以显示每个进程所属的 jail。例如，列出主机上的所有进程及其所属 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1684
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# ps ax -o pid,jail,command\n"
msgstr "# ps ax -o pid,jail,command\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1687
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:top[1] takes `-J` to filter its live display to one jail, which implies "
"`-j` and adds the `JID` column:"
msgstr "man:top[1] 接受 `-J` 参数，可将其实时显示筛选为单个 jail；该参数会隐含启用 `-j`，并添加 `JID` 列："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1691
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# top -J classic\n"
msgstr "# top -J classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1694
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:sockstat[1] lists the sockets belonging to a jail with `-j`, which is "
"the natural way to check which ports a jail's daemons have actually bound "
"after starting a service in it:"
msgstr "man:sockstat[1] 使用 `-j` 列出属于某个 jail 的套接字。在 jail 中启动服务后，这是检查其守护进程实际绑定了哪些端口的常用方法："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1698
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sockstat -4 -6 -l -j classic\n"
msgstr "# sockstat -4 -6 -l -j classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1701
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"From inside a jail the picture is reversed: a jailed process sees only its "
"own jail's processes and sockets, never those of the host or of other jails."
msgstr "在 jail 内部，情况正好相反：jail 中的进程只能看到自身 jail 的进程和套接字，看不到主机或其他 jail 中的内容。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1703
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Managing Jails Directly with the jail Utility"
msgstr "使用 jail 工具直接管理 jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1706
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man:service[8] wrapper shown above is the usual way to run jails at "
"boot, but man:jail[8] can also create, modify, and remove jails directly, "
"which is useful for scripting and for testing a configuration without the rc "
"framework."
msgstr "上文所示的 man:service[8] 封装程序通常用于在启动时运行 jail，但 man:jail[8] 也可以直接创建、修改和移除 jail，适用于编写脚本，以及在不使用 rc 框架的情况下测试配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1708
#, fuzzy
msgid "Create a configured jail by name:"
msgstr "按名称创建已配置的 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1712
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jail -c classic\n"
msgstr "# jail -c classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1715
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Remove a running jail; this also removes any child jails it created and "
"kills the processes inside it:"
msgstr "移除正在运行的 jail；这也会移除它创建的所有子 jail，并结束其中的进程："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1719
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jail -r classic\n"
msgstr "# jail -r classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1723
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `-m` flag modifies the parameters of an already-running jail without "
"restarting it.  For example, to add a second IPv4 address to a running jail:"
msgstr "`-m` 标志可以在不重启 jail 的情况下修改其参数。例如，为正在运行的 jail 添加第二个 IPv4 地址："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1727
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jail -m name=classic ip4.addr+=192.168.250.71\n"
msgstr "# jail -m name=classic ip4.addr+=192.168.250.71\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1730
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:jail[8] notes that \"Some parameters may not be changed on a running jail"
"\"; in practice this includes `path` and `vnet`, which require the jail to "
"be restarted."
msgstr "man:jail[8] 指出：“某些参数无法在 jail 运行时更改”；实际上，这包括 `path` 和 `vnet`，更改它们需要重启 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1733
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Finally, `-e` exhibits all configured non-wildcard jails and their "
"parameters without creating, modifying, or removing anything, which is handy "
"for verifying a configuration file.  It takes a string used to separate the "
"parameters:"
msgstr "最后，`-e` 会显示所有已配置的非通配符 jail 及其参数，而不会创建、修改或移除任何内容，因此很适合用来验证配置文件。该参数接受一个用于分隔参数的字符串："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1737
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# jail -e ,\n"
msgstr "# jail -e ,\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1740
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Creating and Starting a New Jail"
msgid "Backing Up and Migrating a Jail"
msgstr "建立并启动新的Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1743
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A jail is largely self-contained, so backing one up or moving it to another "
"host is mostly a matter of copying its files and its configuration."
msgstr "jail 大多是自包含的，因此备份 jail 或将其迁移到另一台主机，主要就是复制其文件和配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1746
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Stop the jail first for a consistent copy; a ZFS-backed jail can instead be "
"snapshotted while running.  For a jail on its own ZFS dataset, take a "
"recursive snapshot and stream it to the destination host:"
msgstr "为确保副本一致，应先停止 jail；由 ZFS 支持的 jail 也可以在运行时创建快照。对于使用独立 ZFS 数据集的 jail，请创建递归快照，并将其流传输到目标主机："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1752
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# service jail stop classic\n"
"# zfs snapshot -r zroot/jails/containers/classic@migrate\n"
"# zfs send -R zroot/jails/containers/classic@migrate | ssh newhost zfs receive zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# service jail stop classic\n# zfs snapshot -r zroot/jails/containers/classic@migrate\n# zfs send -R zroot/jails/containers/classic@migrate | ssh newhost zfs receive zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1755
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The full mechanics of man:zfs-send[8] and man:zfs-receive[8], including "
"incremental transfers, are covered in crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-send,Replication]."
msgstr "man:zfs-send[8] 和 man:zfs-receive[8] 的完整用法，包括增量传输，详见 crossref:zfs[zfs-zfs-send,Replication]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1757
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For a jail on a UFS file system, use man:tar[1] with `-p` so that ownership, "
"permissions, and file flags are preserved:"
msgstr "对于 UFS 文件系统上的 jail，请使用 man:tar[1] 的 `-p` 选项，以保留所有权、权限和文件标志："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1761
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# tar -cpf classic.tar -C /usr/local/jails/containers classic\n"
msgstr "# tar -cpf classic.tar -C /usr/local/jails/containers classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1765
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Extract the archive as `root` on the destination host with `tar -xpf` so the "
"flags survive.  man:dump[8] and man:restore[8] are an alternative when a "
"jail occupies a dedicated UFS file system of its own; they operate on whole "
"file systems, so they do not apply to the layout used in this chapter, where "
"all jails are directories within one shared file system."
msgstr "在目标主机上以 `root` 身份使用 `tar -xpf` 解压归档，以保留文件标志。如果 jail 使用独立的 UFS 文件系统，也可以使用 man:dump[8] 和 man:restore[8]；但它们针对整个文件系统操作，因此不适用于本章所用的布局，即所有 jail 都是同一共享文件系统中的目录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1767
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Finally, copy the jail's block from [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# — or its "
"file in [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d# — to the new host, adjust any host-"
"specific parameters such as `interface`, `ip4.addr`, or the bridge used by a "
"VNET jail, and start the jail there."
msgstr "最后，将 jail 在 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf# 中的配置块（或其位于 [.filename]#/etc/jail.conf.d# 中的配置文件）复制到新主机，调整 `interface`、`ip4.addr` 或 VNET jail 所用网桥等与主机相关的参数，然后在新主机上启动 jail。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1773
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The destination host must not run an older FreeBSD release than the jail's "
"userland, following the same rule that a jail can never run a newer version "
"than its host.  A NullFS thin jail is not self-contained: its template and "
"skeleton must exist on the destination host too, so migrate those as well or "
"convert the jail to a thick copy first.  Any man:rctl[8] rules kept in [."
"filename]#/etc/rctl.conf# must be carried over separately."
msgstr "目标主机运行的 FreeBSD 版本不得早于 jail 的用户空间版本，这与 jail 不能运行比主机更新的版本遵循同一规则。NullFS thin jail 并非自包含：目标主机上也必须有其模板和骨架，因此请一并迁移它们，或先将该 jail 转换为 thick 副本。保存在 [.filename]#/etc/rctl.conf# 中的任何 man:rctl[8] 规则都必须单独迁移。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1776
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Administration from Inside a Jail"
msgstr "在 jail 内部进行管理"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1780
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most jail administration is done from the host, but some tasks are performed "
"from within the jail itself, and a script running inside a jail sometimes "
"needs to know that it is jailed.  This section describes what an "
"administrator sees and can do from inside a jail."
msgstr "大多数 jail 管理工作都在主机上完成，但有些任务需要在 jail 内执行；在 jail 内运行的脚本有时也需要知道自己是否处于 jail 中。本节介绍管理员在 jail 内部能够看到和执行的内容。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1782
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A process can detect whether it is running inside a jail by reading the "
"`security.jail.jailed` sysctl, which is `1` inside a jail and `0` on the "
"host:"
msgstr "进程可以通过读取 `security.jail.jailed` sysctl 来检测自己是否在 jail 中运行；在 jail 内其值为 `1`，在主机上则为 `0`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1787
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# sysctl security.jail.jailed\n"
"security.jail.jailed: 1\n"
msgstr "# sysctl security.jail.jailed\nsecurity.jail.jailed: 1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1790
#, fuzzy
msgid "Inside a jail the environment is deliberately restricted:"
msgstr "jail 内的环境受到有意限制："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1793
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The host's view of the system is hidden.  A jailed process sees only its own "
"jail's processes, sockets, and file systems, never those of the host or of "
"other jails."
msgstr "主机的系统视图会被隐藏。jail 中的进程只能看到自身 jail 的进程、套接字和文件系统，看不到主机或其他 jail 中的内容。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1795
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kernel state is largely read-only.  Kernel tunables cannot be written from "
"inside a jail, man:kldload[8] and man:kldunload[8] are not permitted, and "
"man:dmesg[8] and the kernel message buffer are unavailable unless `allow."
"read_msgbuf` is set."
msgstr "内核状态大多为只读。无法在 jail 内写入内核可调参数，也不允许使用 man:kldload[8] 和 man:kldunload[8]；除非设置了 `allow.read_msgbuf`，否则也无法使用 man:dmesg[8]，或访问内核消息缓冲区。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1797
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Privileged operations that would cross the jail boundary are denied unless "
"the host explicitly allows them.  Creating raw sockets — as man:ping[8] and "
"man:traceroute[8] require — needs `allow.raw_sockets` (see the parameter "
"description in crossref:jails[jail-configuration-files,Jail Configuration "
"Files]), mounting file systems needs `allow.mount` and its per-filesystem "
"children, and man:chflags[1] is disabled by default (see crossref:jails[jail-"
"upgrading,Jail Upgrading])."
msgstr "除非主机明确允许，否则会拒绝可能跨越 jail 边界的特权操作。创建原始套接字（man:ping[8] 和 man:traceroute[8] 所需）需要设置 `allow.raw_sockets`（参见 crossref:jails[jail-configuration-files,Jail Configuration Files] 中的参数说明）；挂载文件系统需要设置 `allow.mount` 及其各文件系统子参数；man:chflags[1] 默认处于禁用状态（参见 crossref:jails[jail-upgrading,Jail Upgrading]）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1800
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A handful of per-jail sysctl variables can be changed from inside the jail "
"without affecting the host, including `kern.hostname`, `kern.domainname`, "
"`kern.hostid`, `kern.hostuuid`, `kern.securelevel`, and `security.bsd."
"suser_enabled`.  The current set of available jail parameters can be listed "
"with man:sysctl[8]:"
msgstr "少数 jail 专属的 sysctl 变量可以在 jail 内修改，且不会影响主机，包括 `kern.hostname`、`kern.domainname`、`kern.hostid`、`kern.hostuuid`、`kern.securelevel` 和 `security.bsd.suser_enabled`。可以使用 man:sysctl[8] 列出当前可用的 jail 参数："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1804
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# sysctl -d security.jail.param\n"
msgstr "# sysctl -d security.jail.param\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1808
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Managing the jail's own services from inside works exactly as it does on an "
"unjailed system: man:service[8] and man:sysrc[8] operate on the jail's own "
"man:rc[8] configuration.  This is the in-jail counterpart to the host-side "
"crossref:jails[jail-services-host,service -j and sysrc -j] shown above."
msgstr "在 jail 内部管理其自身服务的方式与非 jail 系统完全相同：man:service[8] 和 man:sysrc[8] 操作的是 jail 自己的 man:rc[8] 配置。这是对应于上文所示主机端 crossref:jails[jail-services-host,service -j and sysrc -j] 的 jail 内操作方式。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1810
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Upgrading"
msgid "Jail Upgrading"
msgstr "升级"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1813
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Upgrading FreeBSD Jails ensures that the isolated environments remain "
"secure, up-to-date, and in line with the latest features and improvements "
"available in the FreeBSD ecosystem."
msgstr "升级 FreeBSD Jail 可确保这些隔离环境保持安全、及时更新，并与 FreeBSD 生态系统中最新的功能和改进保持一致。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1819
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The right tool depends on how the jail's userland was installed.  Jails "
"installed from a distribution set (the [.filename]#base.txz# extracted in "
"the creation sections, or one produced by man:bsdinstall[8]) are updated "
"from the host with man:freebsd-update[8] through its `-j` flag, on both "
"FreeBSD 14.x and 15.x.  Jails installed from base packages, available from "
"FreeBSD 15.0, are updated with man:pkg[8] instead; man:freebsd-update[8] "
"does not apply to them.  Jails built from source are updated with the source "
"procedure (`make installworld` and `make distribution`).  Never mix these "
"mechanisms on the same jail."
msgstr "正确的工具取决于 jail 的用户空间是如何安装的。通过发行版集合安装的 jail（在创建章节中解压的 [.filename]#base.txz#，或由 man:bsdinstall[8] 生成的发行版集合）应在主机上使用 man:freebsd-update[8] 的 `-j` 标志进行更新，FreeBSD 14.x 和 15.x 均适用。通过基础软件包安装的 jail（从 FreeBSD 15.0 起可用）则应使用 man:pkg[8] 更新；man:freebsd-update[8] 不适用于它们。通过源代码构建的 jail 应使用源代码更新流程（`make installworld` 和 `make distribution`）。切勿在同一个 jail 上混用这些机制。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1824
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Support for distribution sets is planned for removal in FreeBSD 16, but will "
"continue, together with man:freebsd-update[8], for the lifetime of the "
"FreeBSD 15 stable branch.  Base packages are offered as a technology preview "
"in FreeBSD 15.0 and are expected to become the standard method in future "
"releases, so pkgbase is the forward-looking path."
msgstr "计划在 FreeBSD 16 中移除对发行版集合的支持，但在 FreeBSD 15 稳定分支的整个生命周期内，发行版集合及 man:freebsd-update[8] 都将继续提供。基础软件包在 FreeBSD 15.0 中作为技术预览提供，预计将在未来版本中成为标准方法，因此 pkgbase 是面向未来的选择。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1829
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On OpenZFS, snapshot the jail's dataset before upgrading, so a failed "
"upgrade can be undone instantly:"
msgstr "在 OpenZFS 上，升级前先为 jail 的数据集创建快照，这样升级失败时即可立即撤销："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1833
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/containers/classic@preupgrade\n"
msgstr "# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/containers/classic@preupgrade\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1839
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the upgrade fails, stop the jail and run `zfs rollback zroot/jails/"
"containers/classic@preupgrade` to restore the previous state.  This requires "
"the jail to be its own dataset: the OpenZFS thin-jail clone already is, but "
"a classic jail created with man:mkdir[1] is not, so create it with `zfs "
"create` instead.  For a NullFS thin jail, snapshot the template dataset "
"instead.  man:zfs-rollback[8] reverts only to the most recent snapshot "
"unless `-r` is given to destroy any newer ones."
msgstr "如果升级失败，请停止 jail 并运行 `zfs rollback zroot/jails/containers/classic@preupgrade`，以恢复先前状态。这要求 jail 使用独立的数据集：OpenZFS thin jail 克隆本身就是独立数据集，但使用 man:mkdir[1] 创建的 classic jail 不是，因此应改用 `zfs create` 创建。对于 NullFS thin jail，应为模板数据集创建快照。除非指定 `-r` 以销毁所有较新的快照，否则 man:zfs-rollback[8] 只会回滚到最新的快照。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1842
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Upgrading a Classic Jail or a Thin Jail using OpenZFS Snapshots"
msgstr "使用 OpenZFS 快照升级 Classic Jail 或 Thin Jail"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1847
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Jails *must be updated from the host* operating system.  The default "
"behavior in FreeBSD is to disallow the use of man:chflags[1] in a jail.  "
"This will prevent the update of some files so updating from within the jail "
"will fail."
msgstr "必须从主机操作系统更新 jail。FreeBSD 的默认行为是在 jail 中禁止使用 man:chflags[1]。这会阻止更新某些文件，因此在 jail 内部进行更新将会失败。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1849
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "To update the jail to the latest patch release of the version of FreeBSD "
#| "it is already running, then execute the following commands on the host:"
msgid ""
"To update the jail to the latest patch release of the version of FreeBSD it "
"is running, execute the following commands on the host:"
msgstr "使用主机中最新的 FreeBSD 补丁更新 jail，请在主机中执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1854
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# freebsd-update -j classic fetch install\n"
"# service jail restart classic\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -j classic fetch install\n# service jail restart classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1858
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To upgrade the jail to a new major or minor version, first upgrade the host "
"system as described in crossref:cutting-edge[freebsdupdate-upgrade,"
"\"Performing Major and Minor Version Upgrades\"].  Once the host has been "
"upgraded and rebooted, the jail can then be upgraded."
msgstr "要将 jail 升级到新的主版本或次版本，请先按照 crossref:cutting-edge[freebsdupdate-upgrade,\"Performing Major and Minor Version Upgrades\"] 中的说明升级主机系统。主机升级并重新启动后，即可升级 jail。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1862
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In case of upgrade from one version to another, it is easier to create a new "
"jail than to upgrade completely."
msgstr "从一个版本升级到另一个版本时，创建新的 jail 比彻底升级现有 jail 更简单。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1865
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "To update the jail to the latest patch release of the version of FreeBSD "
#| "it is already running, then execute the following commands on the host:"
msgid ""
"For example, to upgrade the `classic` jail to {rel-latest}-RELEASE, execute "
"the following commands on the host:"
msgstr "使用主机中最新的 FreeBSD 补丁更新 jail，请在主机中执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1873
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# freebsd-update -j classic -r {rel-latest}-RELEASE upgrade\n"
"# freebsd-update -j classic install\n"
"# service jail restart classic\n"
"# freebsd-update -j classic install\n"
"# service jail restart classic\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -j classic -r {rel-latest}-RELEASE upgrade\n# freebsd-update -j classic install\n# service jail restart classic\n# freebsd-update -j classic install\n# service jail restart classic\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1880
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `install` step is run twice on purpose.  A jail has no kernel of its own "
"(it runs the host's kernel), so nothing here upgrades a kernel.  The first "
"`install` writes the new userland into the jail; after the jail restarts on "
"the updated files, the second `install` finishes replacing the components "
"that could not be changed while their previous versions were still in use."
msgstr "有意将 `install` 步骤运行两次。jail 没有自己的内核（它运行的是主机的内核），因此这里不会升级内核。第一次运行 `install` 会将新的用户空间写入 jail；jail 使用更新后的文件重新启动后，第二次运行 `install` 会完成替换那些在旧版本仍在使用时无法更改的组件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1884
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Then, if it was a major version upgrade, reinstall all installed packages "
#| "and restart the jail again. This is required because the ABI version "
#| "changes when upgrading between major versions of FreeBSD. From the host:"
msgid ""
"Then, if it was a major version upgrade, reinstall all installed packages "
"and restart the jail again.  This is required because the ABI version "
"changes when upgrading between major versions of FreeBSD."
msgstr ""
"如果主版本号更新了，重新安装所有软件包并重启 jail。由于FreeBSD 主版本号更新"
"时 ABI 版本也将改变，这部是必须的，在 Host 上执行："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1886
#, fuzzy
msgid "From the host:"
msgstr "在主机上运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1891
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# pkg -j classic upgrade -f\n"
"# service jail restart classic\n"
msgstr "# pkg -j classic upgrade -f\n# service jail restart classic\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1894
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Upgrading OpenZFS Thin Jails"
msgstr "升级 OpenZFS Thin Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1899
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The thin jails created in crossref:jails[creating-thin-jail-openzfs-"
"snapshots,\"Creating a Thin Jail Using OpenZFS Snapshots\"] are OpenZFS "
"clones of a template snapshot, but a clone is independent of that template "
"once it exists.  Refreshing the template does *not* update jails that were "
"already cloned from it, and updating a clone does *not* update the "
"template.  There are therefore two ways to keep these jails current."
msgstr "在 crossref:jails[creating-thin-jail-openzfs-snapshots,\"Creating a Thin Jail Using OpenZFS Snapshots\"] 中创建的 thin jail 是模板快照的 OpenZFS 克隆，但克隆创建后便独立于模板。刷新模板不会更新已经从它克隆出来的 jail，更新克隆也不会更新模板。因此，保持这些 jail 更新有两种方法。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1902
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first option is to update each clone in place with man:freebsd-"
"update[8], exactly as for a classic jail, as described in crossref:"
"jails[jails-updating,\"Upgrading a Classic Jail or a Thin Jail using OpenZFS "
"Snapshots\"].  This is the simplest approach for a handful of jails, but "
"every clone that is patched diverges from the template snapshot: the changed "
"blocks are duplicated per jail, which erodes the space savings, and a major "
"upgrade rewrites so much of the userland that most of the sharing is lost."
msgstr "第一种方法是使用 man:freebsd-update[8] 就地更新每个克隆，操作与 classic jail 完全相同，详见 crossref:jails[jails-updating,\"Upgrading a Classic Jail or a Thin Jail using OpenZFS Snapshots\"]。对于少数几个 jail，这是最简单的方法，但每个经过修补的克隆都会与模板快照产生差异：更改的块会在每个 jail 中重复存储，从而减少空间节省；而主版本升级会重写大量用户空间内容，导致大部分共享空间优势消失。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1905
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The second option keeps the sharing intact by refreshing the template and re-"
"cloning.  Update the template to the latest patch level on the host:"
msgstr "第二种方法通过刷新模板并重新克隆来保持共享不变。在主机上将模板更新到最新的补丁级别："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1915
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:freebsd-update[8] with `-b` reads the running release from the host's "
"`uname -r`, not from the template.  If the template runs an older release "
"than the host, add `--currently-running <template-release>` so it patches "
"the template's release instead of the host's, as shown in crossref:"
"jails[upgrading-thin-jail,\"Upgrading a Thin Jail Using NullFS\"]."
msgstr "man:freebsd-update[8] 使用 `-b` 时，会从主机的 `uname -r` 读取当前运行的发行版，而不是从模板读取。如果模板运行的发行版比主机旧，请添加 `--currently-running <template-release>`，以便修补模板所用的发行版，而不是主机所用的发行版，如 crossref:jails[upgrading-thin-jail,\"Upgrading a Thin Jail Using NullFS\"] 所示。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1918
#, fuzzy
msgid "Then take a new snapshot and clone future jails from it:"
msgstr "然后创建新快照，并从该快照克隆后续 jail："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1923
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base-p2\n"
"# zfs clone zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base-p2 zroot/jails/containers/newjail\n"
msgstr "# zfs snapshot zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base-p2\n# zfs clone zroot/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE@base-p2 zroot/jails/containers/newjail\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1927
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Existing clones keep the base they were created from until they are re-"
"created from the new snapshot.  For a major or minor version upgrade, create "
"a fresh template dataset for the new release following crossref:"
"jails[creating-thin-jail-openzfs-snapshots,\"Creating a Thin Jail Using "
"OpenZFS Snapshots\"], rather than upgrading the existing template in place, "
"and clone new jails from its `@base` snapshot."
msgstr "现有克隆会继续使用创建时所依据的基础版本，直到从新快照重新创建为止。对于主版本或次版本升级，应按照 crossref:jails[creating-thin-jail-openzfs-snapshots,\"Creating a Thin Jail Using OpenZFS Snapshots\"] 中的说明，为新发行版创建一个新的模板数据集，而不是就地升级现有模板，然后从其 `@base` 快照克隆新的 jail。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1931
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Keep each jail's application data and configuration on separate datasets, or "
"in the jail's local storage, so that re-creating a jail from an updated "
"template snapshot is cheap and preferable to patching every clone "
"individually."
msgstr "将每个 jail 的应用程序数据和配置放在单独的数据集中，或放在 jail 的本地存储中，这样就能以较低成本从更新后的模板快照重新创建 jail，而不必逐个修补所有克隆。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1934
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Upgrading a Thin Jail Using NullFS"
msgstr "使用 NullFS 升级 Thin Jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1939
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Since Thin Jails that use NullFS share the majority of system directories, "
"they are very easy to update.  It is enough to update the template.  This "
"allows updating multiple jails at the same time."
msgstr "由于使用 NullFS 的 Thin Jail 共享大部分系统目录，因此更新非常简单。只需更新模板即可。这使得可以同时更新多个 jail。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1941
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "To update the jail to the latest patch release of the version of FreeBSD "
#| "it is already running, then execute the following commands on the host:"
msgid ""
"To update the template to the latest patch release of the version of FreeBSD "
"it is running, execute the following commands on the host:"
msgstr "使用主机中最新的 FreeBSD 补丁更新 jail，请在主机中执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1946
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base/ fetch install\n"
"# service jail restart\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/{rel-latest}-RELEASE-base/ fetch install\n# service jail restart\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1950
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To upgrade the template to a new major or minor version, first upgrade the "
"host system as described in crossref:cutting-edge[freebsdupdate-upgrade,"
"\"Performing Major and Minor Version Upgrades\"].  Once the host has been "
"upgraded and rebooted, the template can then be upgraded."
msgstr "要将模板升级到新的主版本或次版本，请先按照 crossref:cutting-edge[freebsdupdate-upgrade,\"Performing Major and Minor Version Upgrades\"] 中的说明升级主机系统。主机升级并重新启动后，即可升级模板。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1954
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Because the host was upgraded first, man:freebsd-update[8] with `-b` would "
"otherwise detect the host's new release rather than the template's older "
"one: `-b` reads the running version from the host's `uname -r`, unlike `-j`, "
"which detects the jail's own userland.  Pass `--currently-running <template-"
"release>` so the template is patched from its actual release.  The following "
"example upgrades a template running 14.2-RELEASE to 14.3-RELEASE; substitute "
"the releases that apply:"
msgstr "由于先升级了主机，man:freebsd-update[8] 使用 `-b` 时会检测到主机的新发行版，而不是模板的旧发行版：`-b` 从主机的 `uname -r` 读取运行版本，而 `-j` 会检测 jail 自身的用户空间。请传递 `--currently-running <template-release>`，以便根据模板的实际发行版进行修补。以下示例将运行 14.2-RELEASE 的模板升级到 14.3-RELEASE；请替换为适用的发行版："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1962
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/14.2-RELEASE-base/ --currently-running 14.2-RELEASE -r 14.3-RELEASE upgrade\n"
"# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/14.2-RELEASE-base/ install\n"
"# service jail restart\n"
"# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/14.2-RELEASE-base/ install\n"
"# service jail restart\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/14.2-RELEASE-base/ --currently-running 14.2-RELEASE -r 14.3-RELEASE upgrade\n# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/14.2-RELEASE-base/ install\n# service jail restart\n# freebsd-update -b /usr/local/jails/templates/14.2-RELEASE-base/ install\n# service jail restart\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1965
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Updating Multiple Jails"
msgid "Upgrading pkgbase Jails"
msgstr "更新多个 jail"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1968
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Jails installed from base packages, available from FreeBSD 15.0, are "
"upgraded with man:pkg[8] against the `FreeBSD-base` repository rather than "
"with man:freebsd-update[8]."
msgstr "通过基础软件包安装的 jail（从 FreeBSD 15.0 起可用）应使用 man:pkg[8] 从 `FreeBSD-base` 仓库升级，而不是使用 man:freebsd-update[8]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1970
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `FreeBSD-base` repository is defined in [.filename]#/etc/pkg/FreeBSD."
"conf# but is disabled by default on FreeBSD 15.0, so enable it before "
"upgrading."
msgstr "`FreeBSD-base` 仓库定义在 [.filename]#/etc/pkg/FreeBSD.conf# 中，但在 FreeBSD 15.0 上默认禁用，因此升级前应先启用它。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1972
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"From the host, point man:pkg[8] at the jail's root directory with `-r` (`--"
"rootdir`):"
msgstr "在主机上，使用 `-r`（`--rootdir`）将 man:pkg[8] 指向 jail 的根目录："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1978
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# pkg -r /usr/local/jails/containers/pkgjail update\n"
"# pkg -r /usr/local/jails/containers/pkgjail upgrade\n"
"# service jail restart pkgjail\n"
msgstr "# pkg -r /usr/local/jails/containers/pkgjail update\n# pkg -r /usr/local/jails/containers/pkgjail upgrade\n# service jail restart pkgjail\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1981
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The same upgrade can be run from inside the jail with man:jexec[8] and a "
"plain `pkg upgrade`:"
msgstr "也可以在 jail 内使用 man:jexec[8] 和普通的 `pkg upgrade` 执行相同的升级："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1986
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# jexec -l pkgjail pkg upgrade\n"
"# service jail restart pkgjail\n"
msgstr "# jexec -l pkgjail pkg upgrade\n# service jail restart pkgjail\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1993
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:pkg[8] performs a three-way merge on tagged configuration files under [."
"filename]#/etc#.  When a merge cannot be completed automatically it leaves "
"the new version as [.filename]#<file>.pkgnew#, and when it takes over a file "
"that was not previously packaged it saves the old copy as [.filename]#<file>."
"pkgsave#.  Review [.filename]#/etc# after an upgrade and reconcile any such "
"files by hand.  Do not run man:etcupdate[8] on a pkgbase system; man:pkg[8] "
"handles configuration merging itself.  See crossref:cutting-edge[cutting-"
"edge,\"Updating and Upgrading FreeBSD\"] for the host-side base-package "
"workflow."
msgstr "man:pkg[8] 会对 [.filename]#/etc# 下带标签的配置文件执行三方合并。如果无法自动完成合并，它会将新版本保留为 [.filename]#<file>.pkgnew#；如果它接管了以前未打包的文件，则会将旧副本保存为 [.filename]#<file>.pkgsave#。升级后请检查 [.filename]#/etc#，并手动处理这些文件。不要在 pkgbase 系统上运行 man:etcupdate[8]；man:pkg[8] 会自行处理配置合并。有关主机端基础软件包的工作流程，请参见 crossref:cutting-edge[cutting-edge,\"Updating and Upgrading FreeBSD\"]。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1995
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Jail Resource Limits"
msgstr "Jail 资源限制"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:1998
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Controlling the resources that a jail uses from the host system is a task to "
"be taken into account by the system administrator."
msgstr "系统管理员应考虑如何从主机系统控制 jail 使用的资源。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2000
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use man:rctl[8] to manage the resources that a jail can use from the host "
"system."
msgstr "使用 man:rctl[8] 从主机系统管理 jail 可使用的资源。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2004
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `kern.racct.enable` tunable must be enabled at [.filename]#/boot/loader."
"conf#."
msgstr "必须在 [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# 中启用 `kern.racct.enable` 调优参数。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2007
#, fuzzy
msgid "The syntax to limit the resources of a jail is as follows:"
msgstr "限制 jail 资源的语法如下："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2011
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "rctl -a jail:<jailname>:resource:action=amount[/per]\n"
msgstr "rctl -a jail:<jailname>:resource:action=amount[/per]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2016
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The optional `per` component is not a percentage; it is the accounting "
"entity the limit is applied to, one of `process`, `user`, `loginclass`, or "
"`jail`.  For example, `deny=2G/jail` limits the sum for the whole jail, "
"while `deny=2G/process` applies the same figure to each process "
"individually.  A percentage is only meaningful for the `pcpu` resource, "
"whose amount is expressed as a percentage of a single CPU core."
msgstr "可选的 `per` 部分不是百分比，而是应用限制时所针对的记账实体，可以是 `process`、`user`、`loginclass` 或 `jail`。例如，`deny=2G/jail` 限制整个 jail 的总量，而 `deny=2G/process` 则对每个进程分别应用相同的限制值。只有对于 `pcpu` 资源，百分比才有意义；其值表示单个 CPU 核心的百分比。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2018
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For example, to limit the maximum RAM that a jail can access, run the "
"following command:"
msgstr "例如，要限制 jail 可使用的最大 RAM，请运行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2022
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# rctl -a jail:classic:memoryuse:deny=2G\n"
msgstr "# rctl -a jail:classic:memoryuse:deny=2G\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2025
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To make the limitation persistent across reboots of the host system, it will "
"be necessary to add the rule to the [.filename]#/etc/rctl.conf# file as "
"follows:"
msgstr "要使此限制在主机系统重新启动后仍然有效，需要按如下方式将规则添加到 [.filename]#/etc/rctl.conf# 文件中："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2029
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "jail:classic:memoryuse:deny=2G/jail\n"
msgstr "jail:classic:memoryuse:deny=2G/jail\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2034
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:rctl[8] can limit far more than memory.  The resources most relevant to "
"a jail include `pcpu` (percentage of a single CPU core), `maxproc` (number "
"of processes), `openfiles` (open file descriptors), `vmemoryuse` (address "
"space), and `swapuse` (swap space).  Each of them is set the same way:"
msgstr "man:rctl[8] 能限制的资源远不止内存。与 jail 最相关的资源包括 `pcpu`（单个 CPU 核心的百分比）、`maxproc`（进程数）、`openfiles`（打开的文件描述符数）、`vmemoryuse`（地址空间）和 `swapuse`（交换空间）。这些资源的设置方式相同："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2041
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# rctl -a jail:classic:pcpu:deny=80\n"
"# rctl -a jail:classic:maxproc:deny=1000\n"
"# rctl -a jail:classic:openfiles:deny=5000\n"
"# rctl -a jail:classic:vmemoryuse:deny=4G\n"
msgstr "# rctl -a jail:classic:pcpu:deny=80\n# rctl -a jail:classic:maxproc:deny=1000\n# rctl -a jail:classic:openfiles:deny=5000\n# rctl -a jail:classic:vmemoryuse:deny=4G\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2044
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Disk throughput is limited with `readbps` and `writebps`, but these "
"resources do not support the `deny` action; pair them with `throttle` "
"instead:"
msgstr "使用 `readbps` 和 `writebps` 限制磁盘吞吐量，但这些资源不支持 `deny` 操作；应改用 `throttle`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2048
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# rctl -a jail:classic:writebps:throttle=1m\n"
msgstr "# rctl -a jail:classic:writebps:throttle=1m\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2051
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The action after the resource selects what happens when the limit is "
"reached: `deny` blocks the operation, `log` records it to the system log, "
"and `devctl` sends a notification through man:devd[8]."
msgstr "资源后面的操作决定达到限制时的处理方式：`deny` 会阻止操作，`log` 会将其记录到系统日志，而 `devctl` 会通过 man:devd[8] 发送通知。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2053
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Report the current resource usage of a jail with the `-u` flag, adding `-h` "
"for human-readable units:"
msgstr "使用 `-u` 标志报告 jail 当前的资源使用情况；添加 `-h` 可使用易读单位："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2057
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# rctl -hu jail:classic\n"
msgstr "# rctl -hu jail:classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2060
#, fuzzy
msgid "List the rules that apply to a jail:"
msgstr "列出适用于某个 jail 的规则："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2064
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# rctl jail:classic\n"
msgstr "# rctl jail:classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2067
#, fuzzy
msgid "Remove every rule that matches a jail with `-r`:"
msgstr "使用 `-r` 移除匹配某个 jail 的所有规则："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2071
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# rctl -r jail:classic\n"
msgstr "# rctl -r jail:classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2074
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"More information on resource limits can be found in the security chapter in "
"the crossref:security[security-resourcelimits,\"Resource Limits section\"]."
msgstr "有关资源限制的更多信息，请参见安全章节中的 crossref:security[security-resourcelimits,\"Resource Limits section\"]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2076
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "CPU Pinning with cpuset"
msgstr "使用 cpuset 绑定 CPU"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2079
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:rctl[8] with `pcpu` caps how much CPU time a jail may consume, but it "
"does not tie the jail to particular cores; man:cpuset[1] assigns specific "
"cores instead."
msgstr "man:rctl[8] 的 `pcpu` 可以限制 jail 可使用的 CPU 时间，但不会将 jail 绑定到特定核心；man:cpuset[1] 则可分配特定核心。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2081
#, fuzzy
msgid "Restrict a running jail to a set of CPUs by its name or JID:"
msgstr "按名称或 JID 将正在运行的 jail 限制为使用一组指定的 CPU："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2085
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cpuset -l 0-3 -j classic\n"
msgstr "# cpuset -l 0-3 -j classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2088
#, fuzzy
msgid "Query the cores a jail is currently allowed to use with `-g`:"
msgstr "使用 `-g` 查询 jail 当前允许使用的核心："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2092
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cpuset -g -j classic\n"
msgstr "# cpuset -g -j classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2096
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The assigned set is also reported in the cpuset column of `jls -v`.  There "
"is no jail.conf parameter for CPU affinity, so pin the jail at start time by "
"running man:cpuset[1] from an `exec.created` or `exec.poststart` hook, both "
"of which run in the host environment:"
msgstr "分配的集合也会显示在 `jls -v` 的 cpuset 列中。jail.conf 没有用于设置 CPU 亲和性的参数，因此应在启动时通过 `exec.created` 或 `exec.poststart` 钩子运行 man:cpuset[1] 来绑定 jail；这两个钩子都在主机环境中运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2100
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "exec.poststart = \"cpuset -l 0-3 -j classic\";\n"
msgstr "exec.poststart = \"cpuset -l 0-3 -j classic\";\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2103
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Limiting Disk Space"
msgstr "限制磁盘空间"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2107
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:rctl[8] has no resource for filesystem space.  When each jail lives in "
"its own ZFS dataset, cap and guarantee its disk usage with ZFS quotas and "
"reservations instead:"
msgstr "man:rctl[8] 没有用于文件系统空间的资源。如果每个 jail 都位于自己的 ZFS 数据集中，可使用 ZFS 配额和预留空间来限制并保障其磁盘用量："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2112
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# zfs set quota=20G zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"
"# zfs set reservation=5G zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"
msgstr "# zfs set quota=20G zroot/jails/containers/classic\n# zfs set reservation=5G zroot/jails/containers/classic\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2117
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This requires the jail to be a dataset of its own.  The ZFS thin jails "
"created earlier already are, but the Classic Jail procedure creates the jail "
"directory with `mkdir` inside the shared [.filename]#containers# dataset, so "
"create it with `zfs create` first for these commands to apply.  See crossref:"
"jails[host-configuration-directories,\"Setting Up the Jail Directory Tree\"] "
"for the dataset layout and man:zfs-set[8] for the `quota` and `reservation` "
"properties."
msgstr "这要求 jail 本身是一个独立的数据集。前面创建的 ZFS thin jail 已经满足这一点，但 Classic Jail 流程会在共享的 [.filename]#containers# 数据集中使用 `mkdir` 创建 jail 目录，因此要让这些命令适用，需先使用 `zfs create` 创建该数据集。有关数据集布局，请参见 crossref:jails[host-configuration-directories,\"设置 Jail 目录树\"]；有关 `quota` 和 `reservation` 属性，请参见 man:zfs-set[8]。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2119
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "More Jail Options"
msgstr "更多 Jail 选项"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2126
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"man:jail[8] exposes many more parameters than the examples in this chapter "
"use.  A jail is a strong isolation boundary, but it is not an absolute one.  "
"Every `allow.*` relaxation trades isolation for capability and moves the "
"jail's privileged users a step closer to the privileges of the host's "
"`root`.  Grant a jail only the permissions the workload inside it genuinely "
"needs, and leave everything else at its more restrictive default.  The full "
"list is in man:jail[8] and man:jail.conf[5]; the parameters below are the "
"ones an administrator reaches for most often."
msgstr "man:jail[8] 提供的参数远多于本章示例所用的参数。Jail 是一个强大的隔离边界，但并非绝对隔离。每项 `allow.*` 放宽设置都是以隔离性换取能力，并使 jail 中的特权用户更接近主机 `root` 的权限。只授予 jail 内工作负载真正需要的权限，其余一切都保持更严格的默认设置。完整列表见 man:jail[8] 和 man:jail.conf[5]；管理员最常用到的参数如下。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2128
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "The allow.* Permissions"
msgstr "allow.* 权限"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/jails/_index.adoc:2132
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `allow.*` parameters are booleans that hand individual privileges to the "
"jail.  Per man:jail[8], \"With the exception of allow.set_hostname and allow."
"reserved_ports, these boolean parameters are off by default\", so a jail "
"starts locked down and each capability must be granted explicitly."
msgstr "`allow.*` 参数是用于向 jail 授予单项权限的布尔值。根据 man:jail[8]：“除 allow.set_hostname 和 allow.reserved_ports 外，这些布尔参数默认均为关闭”，因此 jail 初始处于锁定状态，必须显式授予每项能力。"

#. type: Block title
